asks.\n# gitStatus\nThis is the git status at the start of the conversation. Note that this status is a snapshot in time, and will not update during the conversation.\n\nCurrent branch: experiments/architecture-and-chaos\n\nMain branch (you will usually use this for PRs): main\n\nGit user: hatif03\n\nStatus:\nM evidence/ledger.jsonl\n M src/storybound/oath/engine.py\n M src/storybound/pipeline.py\n?? evidence/neatlogs/review-3/\n\nRecent commits:\n9356cdd Drill and experiment results so far in the ledger; diagnostic run for the missing picture spans\ndfcad8b Fixes from drills C3 and C4: a judge failover to another family, and an outage shows the try-again screen instead of a refusal\ne918923 Tolerant page parsing for other writer models (found by the Sonnet writer experiment); an independent audit pass for sweeps; the experiment comparison script\n2ec0edb Experiment driver; the reserve Gemini model priced as an assumption\nfe643e3 Experiment tooling: failure injection (chaos), a second judge from another family, a repair-budget setting, ledger fields for the configuration, sweep options\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
