{"parentUuid":"9e66961f-a4e4-4c07-b90e-1f5d3f200431","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d9f2f1c9-21bc-414d-b8fc-f3814127c833","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Overall: finish Storybound for neatHack submission (Mon 12 Oct 2026, window 19:00–23:55 IST). The final demo video is made by the user last; I must only **write the demo video script at the end** (≤3:00, ONE video covering: the problem the agent solves; how cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project; how neatlogs was used to identify and resolve the incidents the agent ran into).\n   - Latest user messages (verbatim intent): \"Solved the remain not solve issues except what I want to do last. Also look in to thi, neatlogs says: Your activity • 22 alerts generated for you • 0 evaluations you completed • 0 comments you posted. Complete the evaluations… The neatlogs team: show how the incidents feature helped identify and solve incidents [demo video at a Drive link I cannot open]… there aren't many incidents on our dashboard, which will not look good… opportunity to experiment with different configurations and agent patterns and different architecture to see what could be and if we are the best at what we can. At the end write a script for the demo video as well.\" Then: \"I have approved neatlogs sign in. Here is a screenshot of the evals page. I have added on detections page and there are three more recommendations. Merge pr3, complete all that is left to do. Resolve this as well: . The orphan-trace and picture-words detection issues are still unresolved. In the diagnostic run, 2 of the 4 painted pictures have no spans in the trace.\"\n   - Standing requests: keep documentation updated always (CLAUDE.md now says so); document how neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai are used; good story for judges (docs/STORY.md); use Trails/runners further; business model/cfo.ai exploration (done); alerts by email (done).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Oath-gated storybook agent (LangGraph); arms B0/B1/B2; deterministic checks + K2 judge with quote check; pipelined review; receipt; GUARDRAIL spans in neatlogs.\n   - Model routing via `STORYBOUND_ROUTES` (role=model); hackathon LiteLLM gateway (Claude/Nova; $20/30 days, 60 rpm); Vertex Gemini; K2 judge; default routes planner nova-2-lite, quiz haiku, picture-text check haiku.\n   - New experiment infrastructure: chaos/failure injection, judge ensemble/failover, repair-budget env, `--audit` residual-break pass, ledger configuration fields, tuning/holdout split.\n   - neatlogs: incidents = triage cards (auto-triggered from detections; statuses open/in_progress/resolved/archived/draft), detections (regex on span types), alerts (channelMask email), evaluations API (form → cohort preview → batch add → launch assignMe → human reviews), MCP helper vs CLI (device login hourly), `traces spans list/payload`.\n   - Entire: Trails with \"Auto build on push\" now ON (trail-review runner passes), `entire review general` findings, Brain facts.\n   - cfo.ai: scenarios for video AI; launch plan; workbooks saved.\n   - Hypothesis for missing spans: neatlogs loses child spans started after the parent span ended (node.settle/node.verify), so async work should be parented to a long-lived span (root workflow context).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `src/storybound/chaos.py` (new): `rules()`, `active()`, `maybe(target)`; hooks in `clients/gemini.py::_call_once` (\"gemini\"), `k2.py::_once` (\"k2\"/\"gateway\"), `gateway.py::_once`, `images.py::_once` (\"image\"), `tts.py::_once` (\"tts\").\n   - `src/storybound/oath/judge.py`: `judge_batch(items,text,context,model=None)`; failover on K2 ClientError to `models.judge_fallback` with `usage.record_fallback(\"judge\", …)`; `ensemble_batch` (strictest verdict wins; one judge's error → other decides); `judge_image` routes `image_no_text` to gateway judge only. Engine default judge = `ensemble_batch`.\n   - `src/storybound/config.py`: `Models.judge_fallback`, `judge_ensemble`, `vision_judge` (default claude-haiku) + `vision_judge_for=(\"image_no_text\",)`, `DEFAULT_ROUTES`, `Thresholds.max_repair_attempts` from STORYBOUND_MAX_REPAIRS, `Settings.hedge_after_s` default 45, `Prices.gateway`, `Prices.gemini_models`.\n   - `src/storybound/pipeline.py`: `unavailable(why)` helper (error event `service_unavailable`), used for `screen_unavailable` and all-verification_error stops; ledger_row adds experiment/chaos/max_repairs/judge_ensemble/hedge_s/routes/split/picture_plan; early painting (`start_painting`, `announce_paint_plan`, `run.early`, `run.paint_set`); `execute()` creates root WORKFLOW span `create-storybook` then `metered()` then `graph.invoke` (copy_context sites at lines ~245, ~516, ~622).\n   - `src/storybound/agents/writer.py`: `normalise()` (unwrap single-key page; build correct/wrong from `choices` with is_correct), `assemble()` error names keys; tests in tests/test_pipeline.py.\n   - `src/storybound/clients/retry.py::hedged` (daemon threads, 45 s), gemini `_call` wrapper records winner usage only; `usage.py` Meter.fallbacks, `record_fallback`, pricing for gateway/gemini_models (unknown gateway model priced at dearest).\n   - `scripts/sweep.py` (`--age --no-judge --media --audit`, `audit_story`), `scripts/run_experiments.py` (EXPERIMENTS table X1–X6, X2b, A0/A4/A5 audits, C1–C7, C3b, C4b, C6), `scripts/compare_experiments.py`, `scripts/regress.py`, `scripts/judge_bias.py`, `scripts/judge_agreement.py`, `scripts/clip_check.py`, `scripts/lint_evidence.py` (docs-freshness checks).\n   - Tests: 99 backend tests pass (chaos, ensemble, failover, error screen, tolerant parsing, hedging, routing, pricing).\n   - Docs/evidence already in repo: HR-001..HR-013, docs/STORY.md, BUSINESS.md, CREDITS.md, LAUNCH-READINESS.md, TOOLS.md (sections 1–6), research notes, `evidence/cfo/workbook/*.xlsx`, `evidence/neatlogs/review-2/`, `review-3/`.\n   - Scratchpad scripts (C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\d--storybound\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6\\scratchpad\\): `make_eval.py` (evaluation creation poller, waits on neatlogs-login9.log), `neatlogs_evals_read.py`, `pick_eval_spans2.py` (CLI picker; found few judge violations), `orphan_test.py`/`orphan_test2.py`, `cmp_routes.py`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Sonnet writer \"page JSON is missing 'correct'\" (3/10 stories errored) → traced in neatlogs (scene_repair returned `choices` list) → `normalise()` fix + keys in error + test; X2b rerun pending/finished unread.\n   - Judge down → 0 stories shipped; safety-screen outage shown as refusal → judge failover + `unavailable()` error screen + tests; C3b/C4b/C7 reruns pending.\n   - Editing `deterministic.py` dropped an import (`instruction_hits`) → NameError seen in 5 test failures → import restored.\n   - `ruff` issues (B007, import order) → fixed.\n   - CLI via Python subprocess gave `MISSING_HOST` because loaded .env set NEATLOGS_* → strip NEATLOGS_* env vars.\n   - neatlogs CLI login expired before evaluation creation → new sign-in needed; poller prepared.\n   - MCP 429 capacity errors → wait ~81 s / use CLI.\n   - Several bash heredoc/escape failures → write scripts to files or use Edit tool.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Experiments produced genuine, trace-visible failures that were fixed (the incident story for the demo: identify in neatlogs → fix → re-run).\n   - Honest findings: Gemini Pro writer improves quality at ~4.7× cost; ensemble judge safe but expensive; repairing (not detecting) keeps promises; hedge saves ~50 s mean under stalls (small n).\n   - Open: why 2 of 4 early-painting `illustrate` spans and all `verify:image_*` spans are missing; orphan one-span traces; picture-words detection blind until spans attach. Next fix hypothesis described above.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Earlier in session, summarized above: history rewrite approval; \"merge pr 2, i have signed in. Complete the rest. for the alert delivery channel, is it possible if every user can set their own? For me my mail md.hatifosmani.15@gmail.com is good enough.\" [email later corrected]; \"The email id on neatlogs would be md.hatifosmani15@gmail.com\" with Entire settings screenshot; \"I have switched on the entire setting. Complete the rest of the still open issues, whatever you can. I have added the sheets from cfo.ai at the root of the project. Also: https://cfo.ai/s/vGE_ZEwfQtpoxPrg\".)\n   - \"Solved the remain not solve issues except what I want to do last. Also look in to thi, neatlogs says… [full text above incl. pasted_content duplicate]\" with 4 screenshots (detections, incidents Open/Investigated/Resolved).\n   - \"I have approved neatlogs sign in. Here is a screenshot of the evals page. I have added on detections page and there are three more recommendations.Merge pr3, complete all that is left to do. Resolve this as well: . The orphan-trace and picture-words detection issues are still unresolved. In the diagnostic run, 2 of the 4 painted pictures have no spans in the trace.\" with 2 screenshots (evals page; detections page with suggestions Response Tagging, Invalid JSON Format Detector, High Token Usage Monitor; table shows Critical Violation Monitor and High Latency LLM Monitor added).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the missing-span/orphan problem (root-context parenting for async tasks), verify with a diagnostic media run, then create/verify the picture-words detection (+ alert) and re-check orphans.\n   - Read round-2 results (X2b, A0/A4/A5 audits, C3b, C4b, C7) and C6; run `scripts/compare_experiments.py --md evidence/experiments/<file>.md`; check whether neatlogs opened new incidents (triage_list); investigate/resolve them with notes (triage_update_status/triage_update/triage_dismiss via MCP helper with user_email md.hatifosmani15@gmail.com).\n   - Write HR-014 (architecture/config experiments incl. audit results) and HR-015 (failure drills and fixes: parser tolerance, judge failover, error screen, hedge result), update docs (STATUS, TOOLS, STORY, QUALIFICATION, LAUNCH-READINESS, API.md `service_unavailable` error code, hackathon.md, CREDITS with measured cost/quality of writers, README/HANDOFF counts, EVIDENCE.md rebuild, lint), possibly a cfo.ai update (writer-model cost rows).\n   - Complete neatlogs evaluations: start a new device login (scopes: context:read organization:read billing:read profile:read observability:read evaluation:read configuration:read sharing:read access:read configuration:write evaluation:write) writing to `evidence/neatlogs-login9.log`, launch `make_eval.py` poller, give the user the verification link at the end; user must label the 20 traces in the dashboard (Assigned to me); consider an AI evaluator evaluation separately (label clearly as AI).\n   - Ask user: screenshot of Assigned-to-me/evals after launch; remind them to click \"Add\" on remaining suggested detections; Entire approvals gate (solo) setting; key rotation; cfo.ai Version-history screenshot; `#neatHack` posts.\n   - Open the experiments branch PR (and merge only if the user asks), run `entire review general` on it, check trail 5 gates.\n   - Write the demo video script (docs/DEMO-SCRIPT.md, ≤3:00): problem; cfo.ai + Entire; neatlogs incidents identified and resolved (include the Sonnet-writer parse incident, judge-outage incident, 504 stall incident, \"hurts\" blocklist incident, with trace ids/evidence paths).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request I was diagnosing why the diagnostic media run (trace `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a`) lacked 2 of 4 `illustrate` spans and all `verify:image_*` spans. After minimal reproductions attached fine, I formed the hypothesis that neatlogs loses children started after their parent node span ended, and had just listed all `copy_context` call sites (pipeline.py:245, 516, 622; engine.py:189; judge.py:149–150; retry.py:61) and `execute()` (lines ~777–800: `@tracing.span(kind=\"WORKFLOW\", name=\"create-storybook\") def _go(): run.trace_id=…; graph=build_graph(run); with metered() as meter: run.meter=meter; graph.invoke(...)`) to plan capturing a root-span context (`run.trace_ctx`) for async work. In parallel, round-2 experiments/drills were running in the background and a neatlogs evaluation-creation poller script (`make_eval.py`) was prepared but the neatlogs login (login9) had not yet been started.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the root-context fix for async tasks, as I was about to do: in `execute()._go()` capture `run.trace_ctx = contextvars.copy_context()` (inside the workflow span, after `metered()`), then replace `contextvars.copy_context().run` with `run.trace_ctx.copy().run` at the pipeline/engine/judge/hedge call sites (engine needs a ctx handle), add a test, run `pytest`, then do a diagnostic run (`STORYBOUND_TAGS=diagnostic scripts/run_story.py benign/bunny-bow-carrot --lesson sharing --media --pictures auto --name diag-spans-2`) and count spans via paged `get_trace_context` (offset) to confirm 4 `illustrate` spans and `verify:image_*` spans, then create the picture-words GUARDRAIL detection if spans appear. Then collect round-2 results, handle new incidents, write HR-014/015 + docs, start the neatlogs login (login9) + `make_eval.py` poller and give the user the link, and finally write `docs/DEMO-SCRIPT.md`. (Verbatim anchor from the user: \"Resolve this as well: . The orphan-trace and picture-words detection issues are still unresolved. In the diagnostic run, 2 of the 4 painted pictures have no spans in the trace.\" and \"complete all that is left to do … At the end write a script for the demo video as well.\")\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\mdhat\\.claude\\projects\\d--storybound\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"aa674112-379a-4a6c-b144-384a217f6c79","timestamp":"2026-10-12T06:46:15.904Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":28,"turnIndex":50},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["9ff67b0b-a3f1-4d0c-a589-55b0c79af466"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"aa674112-379a-4a6c-b144-384a217f6c79","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\d--storybound\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6\\scratchpad\\make_eval.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\d--storybound\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6\\scratchpad\\make_eval.py","content":"import json\nimport os\nimport random\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, r\"D:\\storybound\\src\")\nfrom storybound import ledger  # noqa: E402\n\nN = r\"C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\neatlogs.cmd\"\nEV = \"aea3e3ce-d209-4391-91c4-b7be6844ff07\"\nOUT = Path(r\"D:\\storybound\\evidence\\neatlogs\\review-3\")\nENV = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith(\"NEATLOGS_\")}\n\n\ndef run(args, body=None):\n    p = subprocess.run([N, *args], input=json.dumps(body) if body is not None else None, capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\", timeout=120, env=ENV)\n    return (p.stdout or p.stderr).strip()\n\n\ndef key():\n    return [\"--idempotency-key\", str(uuid.uuid4())]\n\n\nimport time\n\nLOG = Path(\"D:/storybound/evidence/neatlogs-login9.log\")\n_end = time.time() + 3000\nwhile time.time() < _end and not (LOG.exists() and \"credentialSource\" in LOG.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")):\n    time.sleep(10)\nres = {}\nform = {\n    \"name\": \"Do you agree with the story checks?\",\n    \"questions\": [\n        {\"answerType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"questionText\": \"Open the verify:* spans of this story (the oath checks). Do you agree with the verdicts: promises marked kept really are kept, promises marked broken really are broken?\", \"isRequired\": True, \"sortOrder\": 0, \"options\": {\"choices\": [\"Agree with all of them\", \"Disagree with at least one\", \"Cannot tell from the trace\"]}},\n        {\"answerType\": \"paragraph\", \"questionText\": \"If you disagree: which promise, on which page, and why? (Leave empty if you agree.)\", \"isRequired\": False, \"sortOrder\": 1, \"placeholder\": \"e.g. lesson_concept_in_scene on page 3 should have passed because ...\"},\n        {\"answerType\": \"rating\", \"questionText\": \"How suitable is the finished story for a child aged 6? (1 = not at all, 5 = fully)\", \"isRequired\": True, \"sortOrder\": 2, \"options\": {\"min\": 1, \"max\": 5}},\n    ],\n}\nres[\"form\"] = run([\"api\", \"put_api_v1_public_evaluations_evaluationId_form\", \"--param\", f\"evaluationId={EV}\", \"--body-stdin\", *key()], form)\nrows = [r for r in ledger.read() if str(r.get(\"name\", \"\")).startswith((\"X1\", \"X3\", \"X5\", \"X6\", \"holdout-routes-default\", \"age-\")) and r.get(\"trace_id\") and not r.get(\"error\")]\nrandom.seed(5)\nrandom.shuffle(rows)\nrefs = []\nseen = set()\nfor r in rows:\n    if r[\"trace_id\"] in seen:\n        continue\n    seen.add(r[\"trace_id\"])\n    refs.append({\"kind\": \"trace\", \"traceId\": r[\"trace_id\"]})\n    if len(refs) == 20:\n        break\nprev = run([\"api\", \"post_api_v1_public_evaluations_evaluationId_cohort_preview\", \"--param\", f\"evaluationId={EV}\", \"--body-stdin\", *key()], {\"action\": \"add\", \"references\": refs})\nres[\"preview\"] = prev\ntry:\n    h = json.loads(prev)[\"data\"][\"previewHash\"]\n    res[\"add\"] = run([\"api\", \"post_api_v1_public_evaluations_evaluationId_cohort_items_batch_add\", \"--param\", f\"evaluationId={EV}\", \"--body-stdin\", *key()], {\"previewHash\": h, \"references\": refs})\n    res[\"launch\"] = run([\"api\", \"post_api_v1_public_evaluations_evaluationId_launch\", \"--param\", f\"evaluationId={EV}\", \"--body-stdin\", *key()], {\"assignMe\": True, \"reviewDuration\": \"7d\"})\n    res[\"items\"] = run([\"api\", \"get_api_v1_public_evaluations_evaluationId_items\", \"--param\", f\"evaluationId={EV}\"])\n    res[\"assignments\"] = run([\"api\", \"get_api_v1_public_evaluation_assignments\"])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    res[\"error\"] = str(e)\n(OUT / \"eval_create_results.json\").write_text(json.dumps(res, indent=1), encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint({k: v[:400] for k, v in res.items()})\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}},"displayPath":"C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\d--storybound\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6\\scratchpad\\make_eval.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b8f122eb-9521-4a20-94b2-943f6b026772","timestamp":"2026-10-12T06:46:16.435Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\mdhat\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\d--storybound\\\\531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6\\\\scratchpad\\\\make_eval.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\timport json\n2\timport os\n3\timport random\n4\timport subprocess\n5\timport sys\n6\timport uuid\n7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n8\t\n9\tsys.path.insert(0, r\"D:\\storybound\\src\")\n10\tfrom storybound import ledger  # noqa: E402\n11\t\n12\tN = r\"C:\\Users\\mdhat\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\neatlogs.cmd\"\n13\tEV = \"aea3e3ce-d209-4391-91c4-b7be6844ff07\"\n14\tOUT = Path(r\"D:\\storybound\\evidence\\neatlogs\\review-3\")\n15\tENV = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith(\"NEATLOGS_\")}\n16\t\n17\t\n18\tdef run(args, body=None):\n19\t    p = subprocess.run([N, *args], input=json.dumps(body) if body is not None else None, capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\", timeout=120, env=ENV)\n20\t    return (p.stdout or p.stderr).strip()\n21\t\n22\t\n23\tdef key():\n24\t    return [\"--idempotency-key\", str(uuid.uuid4())]\n25\t\n26\t\n27\timport time\n28\t\n29\tLOG = Path(\"D:/storybound/evidence/neatlogs-login9.log\")\n30\t_end = time.time() + 3000\n31\twhile time.time() < _end and not (LOG.exists() and \"credentialSource\" in LOG.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")):\n32\