{"parentUuid":"af136769-98e0-4918-a1aa-ef5ca6df20b0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6f9d35b9-278f-4396-aeb9-e71bdbc18fe9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpzVWiyqvyGSwvQdvJjGfG","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"code\":\"NOT_FOUND\",\"detail\":\"The requested public API resource was not found.\",\"instance\":\"/api/v1/public/evaluations/aea3e3ce-d209-4391-91c4-b7be6844ff07/form\",\"requestId\":\"req_f00187bfe1065633418d355e2ba93f74\"}\n{\"data\":{\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-11T03:38:26.484Z\",\"id\":\"aea3e3ce-d209-4391-91c4-b7be6844ff07\",\"isRecurring\":false,\"name\":\"Human review of judge verdicts\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"traceSource\":\"existing\",\"type\":\"human\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-11T03:38:26.484Z\",\"batchSchedule\":null,\"dailyLimit\":null,\"description\":\"Twenty judged story pages: does a human agree with the K2 judge on each promise (quote shown)? Compares human and judge to measure agreement.\",\"endsAt\":null,\"nextBatchAt\":null,\"notificationConfig\":null,\"queuedItemCount\":0,\"reminderConfig\":null,\"reviewDeadline\":null,\"reviewDuration\":\"7d\",\"samplingRate\":100,\"sendFrequency\":\"manual\",\"sentAt\":null,\"startsAt\":null,\"traceFilter\":null},\"requestId\":\"req_ebd0316207d4353e672a4841ad51c44f\",\"success\":true}\n{\"data\":{\"evaluations\":[{\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-11T03:38:26.484Z\",\"id\":\"aea3e3ce-d209-4391-91c4-b7be6844ff07\",\"isRecurring\":false,\"name\":\"Human review of judge verdicts\",\"status\":\"draft\",\"traceSource\":\"existing\",\"type\":\"human\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-11T03:38:26.484Z\"}],\"page\":{\"hasMore\":false,\"limit\":50,\"nextCursor\":null}},\"requestId\":\"req_8556ab4da41f8c4272246fe9f658fbdd\",\"success\":true}      1 evaluations API (form → cohort preview → batch add → launch assignMe → human reviews), MCP helper vs CLI (device login hourly), `traces spans list/payload`.\\n   - Entire: Trails with \\\n      1 evaluations yet.\\n  - Auto-imported prompt versions exist.\\n  - Creating evaluations, alerts or sharing links needs a write-scope login, or the dashboard.\\n- **Entire:** `why`, graph-diff and token evidence for the newer fixes are saved.\\n- **Tests and commits:** 77 backend and 19 web tests pass, and everything is committed locally. Five commits are not yet pushed.\\n\\n**Still open:**\\n- **Judge-reviewed quiz questions:** a fresh review of questions from several stories, to measure how often they're repaired or dropped.\\n- **Entire:** the Trails access form, and testing the checkpoint link as a judge.\\n- **neatlogs:** creating evaluations and alerts needs your write access or the dashboard.\\n- **Teacher-written promises:** these work end to end, but there's no editing UI beyond three text fields.\\n- **Final demo video:** you asked for this last.\\n\\nPlease rotate the two keys you pasted (neatlogs and the hackathon gateway) before any push, since several checkpoints now contain them.\n      2 evaluations | Read trace/span-linked evaluation questions, human/AI answers and all related judge runs, including pending/fa\\r\\nget_project_analytics | Read scoped analytics dashboard aggregates over explicit [from,to) windows (max 30 days). kpis returns exact p\\r\\nget_detection_capabilities | Discover native detection config/code input schemas and authoring guidance, plus existing project monitoring. \\r\\nget_detection_status | Read a project's saved detection configuration/activation and native backfill status/progress/token. Null or p\\r\\ntriage_list | List fixes (issues the platform has detected and queued for the team to act on) for the project. Each fix has \\r\\ntriage_get | Get the full fix: root cause, evidence, recommended action (steps, verification, risk assessment, rollback pla\\r\\ntriage_get_investigation | Fetch the full investigation that produced a fix: orchestrator steps, the final fix (if any), and basic info o\\r\\ntriage_list_steps | List the investigation steps (root-cause reasoning trail) attached to a fix. Each step is one tool call / LLM \\r\\ntriage_list_versions | List the saved content versions of a fix's editable sections (root cause, evidence, recommended action). Every\\r\\ntriage_get_version | Fetch a single saved version snapshot of a fix's editable content (root cause, evidence, recommended action) b\\r\\ntriage_accept | Traceback (most recent call last):\\r\\n  File \\\n      2 evaluations, analytics, prompts,\\nskills, and other authorized resources; choose the exact operation and minimum\\nscope for the user's task. Request or perform mutations only when the user\\nauthorized them and the target deployment permits them.\\n\\nBackend contract: [Public API v1](https://github.com/neatlogs/neatlogs-app/blob/7253b22987c749cb4b1b50c063f6903c313273d3/backend/docs/public-api/v1.md).\\nCLI source: [command reference](https://github.com/neatlogs/neatlogs-app/blob/7253b22987c749cb4b1b50c063f6903c313273d3/cli/docs/command-reference.md).\n      2 evaluations, scores, annotations, or feedback · **[INV]** investigations · **[ALERT]** alerts · **[SESS]** sessions · **[SHARE]** sharing · **[CC]** Claude Code · **[PROMPT]** prompts or experiments · **[LEGACY]** legacy\\n\\n## Docs: Overview, Quickstart, Guides\\n- **Welcome to Neatlogs**: Overview of observability for agent runs.\\n- **Introduction**: Starting point for new users.\\n- **Instrument with the Wizard**: Adds Neatlogs to a project with one command.\\n- **Explore the Dashboard**: Tour of what appears once traces arrive.\\n- **Import Traces**: Brings in traces from Langfuse, LangSmith, and others.\\n- **FAQ**: Common questions and troubleshooting.\\n- **Guides** (index): End-to-end tracing recipes.\\n- **RAG Pipeline**: Tracing a retrieval-augmented generation pipeline.\\n- **Multi-Agent LangGraph**: Tracing a LangGraph multi-agent workflow.\\n- **CrewAI Multi-Agent Crew**: Tracing a CrewAI crew with per-agent prompt templates. **[PROMPT]**\\n- **Custom Orchestration**: Tracing a pure Python agent with no framework.\\n- **Chatbot Sessions**: Grouping multi-turn chatbot traces into one session. **[SESS]**\\n- **Long Running Sessions Integration**: Real-time monitoring of long-running sessions. **[SESS]**\\n- **MCP Integration**: Connecting agents and IDEs via the Model Context Protocol.\\n- **llms.txt File**: Machine-readable docs index.\\n\\n## Features\\n- **Traces**: View and analyze agent run traces.\\n- **Session Replay** **[SESS]**: Step-by-step playback of an agent session.\\n- **Comments** **[EVAL]**: Collaborate on traces inside the product.\\n- **Detections**: Auto-flag traces matching conditions or patterns.\\n- **Investigate** **[INV]**: Neat AI runs multi-step investigations of traces.\\n- **Tools & MCPs**: Connect external apps such as GitHub, Linear, and Slack.\\n- **Analytics**: Dashboards for cost, latency, errors, and tools.\\n- **Fixes**: AI-generated fix suggestions for failing traces.\\n- **Experiments** **[PROMPT]**: Prompt version control and a sandbox for testing changes.\\n- **Evals** **[EVAL]**: Route traces to human or AI reviewers with a rubric.\\n- **Human Evaluators** **[EVAL]**: Assign traces to team members and collect judgments.\\n- **AI Evaluators** **[EVAL]**: Configure an LLM or agent judge with your own rubric.\\n- **Alerts** **[ALERT]**: Notifications when detections fire or metrics cross thresholds.\\n- **Integrations**: Connect issue trackers, chat, and similar tools.\\n\\n## SDK\\n- **SDK Overview**: Choosing a platform and instrumenting an app.\\n- **Python SDK**: Install, initialize, and instrument.\\n- **TypeScript SDK**: Install, initialize, and instrument Node.js apps.\\n- **Go SDK**: Install, initialize, and instrument Go apps.\\n- **SDK Doctor**: Local validation of the installed SDK.\\n- **Browser SDK**: Send traces from front-end apps.\\n- **HTTP Trace Injection**: Send traces over plain HTTP without an SDK.\\n- **OpenTelemetry (OTLP)**: Point OTel exporters at Neatlogs.\\n- **Distributed Tracing**: Continue one trace across service boundaries.\\n- **Sessions** **[SESS]**: Group traces from one conversation.\\n- **Tags**: Labels for filtering and grouping traces.\\n- **Workflow Name**: Organizing traces by workflow.\\n- **Multiple Workflows in One Codebase**: Separate workflows within one process.\\n- **Secondary Clients**: Send some traces to another project.\\n- **Flush and Shutdown**: Draining telemetry in scripts and servers.\\n- **Custom Attributes**: `neatlogs.*` attributes for span types.\\n- **Prompt Templates and Managed Prompts** **[PROMPT]**: Tracking templates in telemetry and managing prompts.\\n- **PII Redaction**: Automatic redaction of personal data.\\n- **End-User Identity**: Attaching end-user IDs to traces.\\n- **Span Kinds**: Semantic labels for span roles.\\n- **Python Auto-Instrumentation**: Supported library keys and install commands.\\n\\n## Integrations\\n- **Integrations** (index): Overview of supported providers and frameworks.\\n- **OpenAI**, **Anthropic**, **Google Gemini**, **Azure OpenAI**, **AWS Bedrock**, **Vertex AI**, **OpenRouter**: Model provider tracing in Python and/or TypeScript.\\n- **LangChain**, **CrewAI**, **Mastra**, **Vercel AI SDK**, **Pydantic AI**, **DSPy**, **Agno**, **Strands**, **Google ADK**, **OpenAI Agents SDK**, **Hermes**: Agent framework tracing.\\n- **Pi Agent** **[LEGACY]**: Covers maintained and legacy Pi Agent apps.\\n- **Claude Agent SDK** **[CC]**: Tracing the Claude Agent SDK in Python and TypeScript.\\n- **Claude Code Plugin** **[CC]**: Captures each Claude Code session as a trace.\\n- **Codex Hooks**: Captures Codex coding sessions as traces.\\n- **opencode Plugin**: Captures opencode sessions as traces.\\n- **Agent Skills**: Teaches a coding agent to instrument code.\\n- **MCP Server**: Lets a coding agent query traces, detections, and related data.\\n- **MCP Tools Reference**: Schemas and examples for MCP tools.\\n\\n## CLI\\n- **NeatLogs CLI**, **Tested CLI workflows**, **Project, evaluation and cl