{"parentUuid":"2ad293b5-1b73-4e64-a109-54140e94920e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwv4XC3KqVYczoHGkDcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status so far:\n\n- **Missing picture spans: fixed.** The new diagnostic trace has all 4 `illustrate` spans and 8 picture-check spans under one root. Before, it had 2 and 0. Committed as `74349c9` with a test, and 100 tests pass.\n- **Picture-words detection:** it already existed and its pattern matches a violation but not a pass. It can now see picture checks, but this run had no violation to fire on.\n- **neatlogs evaluation:** launched with 19 traces assigned to you. One of the 20 picked traces was rejected by neatlogs.\n- **New incidents:** the three open cards were not what they claimed.\n  - The \"infinite repair loop\" card: the repair cap holds, and its linked traces were fragments from the span bug.\n  - The `illustrate` latency card: that was our own image-429 drill, and the agent recovered as designed.\n  - The K2 prose card: the linked K2 output was valid JSON only.\n  - All three are resolved with notes.\n- **Still running:** round-2 experiments (audits and failure drills). When they finish I'll count orphan traces after the fix, then write HR-014/015/016, update the docs and write the demo script.\n\n**To finish the evaluation, please open neatlogs → Evals → Assigned to me and label the 19 traces.** Each takes a minute: do you agree with the story checks, why if not, and how suitable the story is for a 6-year-old."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":125109,"output_tokens":622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":148},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_