{"parentUuid":"0647c5ea-c040-422d-8eb1-28638a6bdf7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyMJZLj4BaWHY938PGu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":170031,"output_tokens":1646,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":53},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1646,"cache_read_input_tokens":170031,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":657,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"0561c175-c159-4ab5-aba5-3f90180c630f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwyMHyrvwuiyUKEjYHZL","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"26ec08e5-205e-463a-b8e6-96b616ebefb4","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:28.119Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"26ec08e5-205e-463a-b8e6-96b616ebefb4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyMJZLj4BaWHY938PGu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T1ZfU7wpRvaQDNnxTVw4Lv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\evidence\\hardening\\HR-015.md","content":"# HR-015: failure drills, and the four things they broke\n\nDate: 12 Oct 2026. Our dashboard had few incidents, so we made some on purpose: `src/storybound/chaos.py` injects a failure (a stall, an error code, an outage) into one service for a run (`STORYBOUND_CHAOS=service:kind:value:probability`), the runs are tagged `chaos` in neatlogs, and each row in `evidence/ledger.jsonl` carries the setting. Five stories per drill (`scripts/run_experiments.py`), results in [20261012-comparison.md](../experiments/20261012-comparison.md).\n\n## The drills and what they showed\n| Drill | Failure injected | Result | What it found |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C1 / C2 | Gemini stalls for 100 s on 15% of calls, hedged retry on / off | 5 of 5 shipped both ways; mean 244 s against 294 s (longest 471 s against 415 s) | The hedge saves about 50 s on average; five stories each is too few to call it more |\n| C3 | Gemini returns 503 on 40% of calls | 4 shipped, **1 shown a refusal** | An outage of the safety screen was shown to the child as \"your picture was refused\" |\n| C3b | the same, after the fix | 4 shipped, **1 generic error** | A 503 that outlasted its retries in the character reader escaped as \"something went wrong\" |\n| C4 | K2 (the judge) is down | **0 of 5 shipped:** 3 stopped, 1 refused, 1 error | One judge is a single point of failure; no story could be checked, so none was shown |\n| C4b | K2 down, after the failover | 5 of 5 shipped, checked by the judge from another family ($0.129 a story, 5 times the usual) | The receipt says the judge changed |\n| C5 | the model gateway is down | 5 of 5 shipped | Routes fall back to Gemini; no harm |\n| C6 | image model returns 429 on 80% of calls | 2 shipped, 1 shipped with notes, 12 pictures failed; the whole run took 23 minutes | The agent falls back to a second image model and ships text-only pages when pictures cannot be painted; slow when the image service is the one failing |\n| C7 | K2 and the gateway judge are both down | 5 of 5 stopped at the try-again screen, nothing unchecked shown | The safe failure: no verdict, no story |\n\n## The four things found, and the fixes\n1. **A page-JSON mismatch from a stronger writer** (X2, HR-014): Claude Sonnet's repair call returned the two answers as a `choices` list; the parser wanted `correct` and `wrong`, and 3 of 10 stories ended in an error. Found in neatlogs by opening the error spans; `writer.normalise()` now accepts both shapes and the error names the keys it saw. After the fix: 10 of 10 (X2b). Test: `tests/test_pipeline.py`.\n2. **A judge outage was a dead end** (C4): the agent had one judge. Now a K2 error fails over to a judge from another family (`models.judge_fallback`), the receipt records the fallback, and a run where every judge fails stops at the try-again screen (C7).\n3. **A service outage looked like a refusal** (C3): a screen that could not run was reported as unsafe. It is now `screen_unavailable`, and the child sees \"Pip is having trouble right now. Please try again in a minute.\" (error code `service_unavailable`, documented in `docs/API.md`), never a refusal.\n4. **A model error that outlived its retries escaped as a generic error** (C3b): `execute()` now maps any such error to the same try-again screen. Test: `test_a_model_service_that_fails_after_its_retries_shows_the_try_again_screen`.\n\n## Limits, said plainly\nFive stories per drill; the drills were run before and after the fixes on the same five drawings, so the \"after\" rows are a re-test of the same cases, not a fresh sample. The stall drill's saving (about 50 s) is within the spread of the runs. C6's 23 minutes is a real weakness: with the image service failing, the child waits for pictures that may not come; the text pages are ready much earlier, and a hard time budget for pictures is not built.\n\n## Regression fixture\n`python scripts/run_experiments.py --only C3b,C4b,C7`; unit tests for each fix in `tests/test_pipeline.py` and `tests/test_judge.py`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":170031,"output_tokens":1646,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":53},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1646,"cache_read_input_tokens":170031,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01T1ZfU7wpRvaQDNnxTVw4Lv":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\evidence\\hardening\\HR-015.md","content":"# HR-015: failure drills, and the four things they broke\n\nDate: 12 Oct 2026. Our dashboard had few incidents, so we made some on purpose: `src/storybound/chaos.py` injects a failure (a stall, an error code, an outage) into one service for a run (`STORYBOUND_CHAOS=service:kind:value:probability`), the runs are tagged `chaos` in neatlogs, and each row in `evidence/ledger.jsonl` carries the setting. Five stories per drill (`scripts/run_experiments.py`), results in [20261012-comparison.md](../experiments/20261012-comparison.md).\n\n## The drills and what they showed\n| Drill | Failure injected | Result | What it found |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C1 / C2 | Gemini stalls for 100 s on 15% of calls, hedged retry on / off | 5 of 5 shipped both ways; mean 244 s against 294 s (longest 471 s against 415 s) | The hedge saves about 50 s on average; five stories each is too few to call it more |\n| C3 | Gemini returns 503 on 40% of calls | 4 shipped, **1 shown a refusal** | An outage of the safety screen was shown to the child as \"your picture was refused\" |\n| C3b | the same, after the fix | 4 shipped, **1 generic error** | A 503 that outlasted its retries in the character reader escaped as \"something went wrong\" |\n| C4 | K2 (the judge) is down | **0 of 5 shipped:** 3 stopped, 1 refused, 1 error | One judge is a single point of failure; no story could be checked, so none was shown |\n| C4b | K2 down, after the failover | 5 of 5 shipped, checked by the judge from another family ($0.129 a story, 5 times the usual) | The receipt says the judge changed |\n| C5 | the model gateway is down | 5 of 5 shipped | Routes fall back to Gemini; no harm |\n| C6 | image model returns 429 on 80% of calls | 2 shipped, 1 shipped with notes, 12 pictures failed; the whole run took 23 minutes | The agent falls back to a second image model and ships text-only pages when pictures cannot be painted; slow when the image service is the one failing |\n| C7 | K2 and the gateway judge are both down | 5 of 5 stopped at the try-again screen, nothing unchecked shown | The safe failure: no verdict, no story |\n\n## The four things found, and the fixes\n1. **A page-JSON mismatch from a stronger writer** (X2, HR-014): Claude Sonnet's repair call returned the two answers as a `choices` list; the parser wanted `correct` and `wrong`, and 3 of 10 stories ended in an error. Found in neatlogs by opening the error spans; `writer.normalise()` now accepts both shapes and the error names the keys it saw. After the fix: 10 of 10 (X2b). Test: `tests/test_pipeline.py`.\n2. **A judge outage was a dead end** (C4): the agent had one judge. Now a K2 error fails over to a judge from another family (`models.judge_fallback`), the receipt records the fallback, and a run where every judge fails stops at the try-again screen (C7).\n3. **A service outage looked like a refusal** (C3): a screen that could not run was reported as unsafe. It is now `screen_unavailable`, and the child sees \"Pip is having trouble right now. Please try again in a minute.\" (error code `service_unavailable`, documented in `docs/API.md`), never a refusal.\n4. **A model error that outlived its retries escaped as a generic error** (C3b): `execute()` now maps any such error to the same try-again screen. Test: `test_a_model_service_that_fails_after_its_retries_shows_the_try_again_screen`.\n\n## Limits, said plainly\nFive stories per drill; the drills were run before and after the fixes on the same five drawings, so the \"after\" rows are a re-test of the same cases, not a fresh sample. The stall drill's saving (about 50 s) is within the spread of the runs. C6's 23 minutes is a real weakness: with the image service failing, the child waits for pictures that may not come; the text pages are ready much earlier, and a hard time budget for pictures is not built.\n\n## Regression fixture\n`python scripts/run_experiments.py --only C3b,C4b,C7`; unit tests for each fix in `tests/test_pipeline.py` and `tests/test_judge.py`.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0561c175-c159-4ab5-aba5-3f90180c630f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwyMHyrvwuiyUKEjYHZL","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aedaa1c5-d4ff-4157-a874-d3a48e25c4aa","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:39.350Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
