ften C5 claim and check poller"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01KdsJxJrdDaqTPJ9n5aVCLC":{"cwd":"/d/storybound"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c64e0959-4246-4cb7-bb13-11437fff3d8c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwyNLi72fjQ5N7QFaPum","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0789ebbf-7333-48ab-ae6f-b3a468479687","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:44.313Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"0789ebbf-7333-48ab-ae6f-b3a468479687","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93599b87-86af-4de1-a515-88e8eaaaeeca","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KdsJxJrdDaqTPJ9n5aVCLC","type":"tool_result","content":"Mon Oct 12 07:46:45 UTC 2026","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"59f565f9-a012-4d7f-8d6b-6f9a651c52ff","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:45.051Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Mon Oct 12 07:46:45 UTC 2026","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c64e0959-4246-4cb7-bb13-11437fff3d8c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/d/storybound","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0789ebbf-7333-48ab-ae6f-b3a468479687","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"59f565f9-a012-4d7f-8d6b-6f9a651c52ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"D:\\storybound\\evidence\\hardening\\HR-015.md","snippet":"5\t## The drills and what they showed\n6\t| Drill | Failure injected | Result | What it found |\n7\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n8\t| C1 / C2 | Gemini stalls for 100 s on 15% of calls, hedged retry on / off | 5 of 5 shipped both ways; mean 244 s against 294 s (longest 471 s against 415 s) | The hedge saves about 50 s on average; five stories each is too few to call it more |\n9\t| C3 | Gemini returns 503 on 40% of calls | 4 shipped, **1 shown a refusal** | An outage of the safety screen was shown to the child as \"your picture was refused\" |\n10\t| C3b | the same, after the fix | 4 shipped, **1 generic error** | A 503 that outlasted its retries in the character reader escaped as \"something went wrong\" |\n11\t| C4 | K2 (the judge) is down | **0 of 5 shipped:** 3 stopped, 1 refused, 1 error | One judge is a single point of failure; no story could be checked, so none was shown |\n12\t| C4b | K2 down, after the failover | 5 of 5 shipped, checked by the judge from another family ($0.129 a story, 5 times the usual) | The receipt says the judge changed |\n13\t| C5 | the model gateway is down | 5 of 5 shipped | The gateway roles (planner, quiz, picture-text check) fell back to another model; $0.016 a story, no harm seen |\n14\t| C6 | image model returns 429 on 80% of calls | 2 shipped, 1 shipped with notes, 12 pictures failed; the whole run took 23 minutes | The agent falls back to a second image model and ships text-only pages when pictures cannot be painted; slow when the image service is the one failing |\n15\t| C7 | K2 and the gateway judge are both down | 5 of 5 stopped at the try-again screen, nothing unchecked shown | The safe failure: no verdict, no story |\n16\t\n17\t## The four things found, and the fixes\n18\t1. **A page-JSON mismatch from a stronger writer** (X2, HR-014): Claude Sonnet's repair call returned the two answers as a `choices` list; the parser wanted `correct` and `wrong`, and 3 of 10 stories ended in an error. Found in neatlogs by opening the error spans; `writer.normalise()` now accepts both shapes and the error names the keys it saw. After the fix: 10 of 10 (X2b). Test: `tests/test_pipeline.py`.\n19\t2. **A judge outage was a dead end** (C4): the agent had one judge. Now a K2 error fails over to a judge from another family (`models.judge_fallback`), the receipt records the fallback, and a run where every judge fails stops at the try-again screen (C7).\n20\t3. **A service outage looked like a refusal** (C3): a screen that could not run was reported as unsafe. It is now `screen_unavailable`, and the child sees \"Pip is having trouble right now. Please try again in a minute.\" (error code `service_unavailable`, documented in `docs/API.md`), never a refusal.\n21\t4. **A model error that outlived its retries escaped as a generic error** (C3b): `execute()` now maps any such error to the same try-again screen. Test: `test_a_model_service_that_fails_after_its_retries_shows_the_try_again_screen`."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f0b1664c-d440-473d-ad3a-58c5943805e9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:46:45.088Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: D:\\storybound\\evidence\\hardening\\HR-015.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n5\t## The drills and what they showed\n6\t| Drill | Failure injected | Result | What it found |\n7\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n8\t| C1 / C2 | Gemini stalls for 100 s on 15% of calls, hedged retry on / off | 5 of 5 shipped both ways; mean 244 s against 294 s (longest 471 s against 415 s) | The hedge saves about 50 s on average; five stories each is too few to call it more |\n9\t| C3 | Gemini returns 503 on 40% of calls | 4 shipped, **1 shown a refusal** | An outage of the safety screen was shown to the child as \"your picture was refused\" |\n10\t| C3b | the same, after the fix | 4 shipped, **1 generic error** | A 503 that outlasted its retries in the character reader escaped as \"something went wrong\" |\n11\t| C4 | K2 (the judge) is down | **0 of 5 shipped:** 3 stopped, 1 refused, 1 error | One judge is a single point of failure; no story could be checked, so none was shown |\n12\t| C4b | K2 down, after the failover | 5 of 5 shipped, checked by the judge from another family ($0.129 a story, 5 times the usual) | The receipt says the judge changed |\n13\t| C5 | the model gateway is down | 5 of 5 shipped | The gateway roles (planner, quiz, picture-text check) fell back to another model; $0.016 a story, no harm seen |\n14\t| C6 | image model returns 429 on 80% of calls | 2 shipped, 1 shipped with notes, 12 pictures failed; the whole run took 23 minutes | The agent falls back to a second image model and ships text-only pages when pictures cannot be painted; slow when the image service is the one failing |\n15\t| C7 | K2 and the gateway judge are both down | 5 of 5 stopped at the try-again screen, nothing unchecked shown | The safe failure: no verdict, no story |\n16\t\n17\t## The four things found, and the fixes\n18\t1. **A page-JSON mismatch from a stronger writer** (X2, HR-014): Claude Sonnet's repair call returned the two answers as a `choices` list; the parser wanted `correct` and `wrong`, and 3 of 10 stories ended in an error. Found in neatlogs by opening the error spans; `writer.normalise()` now accepts both shapes and the error names the keys it saw. After the fix: 10 of 10 (X2b). Test: `tests/test_pipeline.py`.\n19\t2. **A judge outage was a dead end** (C4): the agent had one judge. Now a K2 error fails over to a judge from another family (`models.judge_fallback`), the receipt records the fallback, and a run where every judge fails stops at the try-again screen (C7).\n20\t3. **A service outage looked like a refusal** (C3): a screen that could not run was reported as unsafe. It is now `screen_unavailable`, and the child sees \"Pip is having trouble right now. Please try again in a minute.\" (error code `service_unavailable`, documented in `docs/API.md`), never a refusal.\n21\t4. **A model error that outlived its retries escaped as a generic error** (C3b): `execute()` now maps any such error to the same try-again screen. Test: `test_a_model_service_that_fails_after_its_retries_shows_the_try_again_screen`.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
