{"parentUuid":"61f0f74e-851b-4f5c-b2b5-7f39e5467725","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93599b87-86af-4de1-a515-88e8eaaaeeca","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QwDF5dA2xDnUu6ZZqfcxAP","type":"tool_result","content":"- What failed or was confounded: the first regression run and the first reading-pace browser run overlapped other jobs and are marked as such; two browser scripts needed fixes (ghost-tap lock, order game after the quiz); the first live \"after\" run clicked through at machine speed and was not used.\n- Tests that ran: 85 backend, 26 web, 11 touch browser checks, `lint_evidence.py` 0 FAIL. Not run: a real iPad, a real pencil, Safari, a non-English drawing, ages 4 and 8.\n\n### 2026-10-11, afternoon IST (second part): neatlogs review, credits, video futures, a product plan\n- Asked for: a cfo.ai plan if we ever used video AI; the ways we use neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai documented and kept current; the business model and what it takes to make a product; a pass through neatlogs incidents, traces, detections, alerts and analytics; spreading the Gemini load onto the hackathon credits; better use of Trails and runners; a story of how the three tools helped.\n- Ran: neatlogs MCP reads (analytics, detections, triage, traces) and a subagent review: the 87 s stall is back in bursts, two detections never fired, no alert can notify anyone, 9 of 13 critical stops were false positives before HR-004 (HR-011: hedged retry, \"ignore all\" tiered, quiz detection recreated on GUARDRAIL spans, `STORYBOUND_TAGS`). Gateway routing experiments on 10 held-out stories per profile (HR-012): writer on Haiku shipped a break in 3 of 10; character card on Haiku misread a carrot as an ice-cream cone; safety screen on Haiku 23 of 26; planner on Nova 2 Lite plus quiz maker on Haiku is not distinguishable from all-Gemini at n = 10 and is now the default; judge agreement of three Claude models with K2 (Sonnet 65 of 72, Opus 61 of 72, Haiku 60 of 69; every difference on the borderline promise; recomputed after Entire's review found error cells counted as passes). cfo.ai: four Video AI scenarios and a Launch plan page (changes 279505 to 279519). Brain: six facts; a graph diff. New docs: STORY, BUSINESS, CREDITS; lint now warns when docs lag the code.\n- Failed or limited: the first distributed-profile live run (character card on Haiku) shipped 7 breaks and cost $0.69; neatlogs CLI login expired so alert thresholds were not retuned; the picture-words detection could not be previewed; orphan one-span traces not explained; ten stories per profile is a small sample.\n- Tests that ran: 91 backend; lint_evidence 0 FAIL. Not run: a real iPad, ages 4 and 8, a non-English drawing.\n\n### 2026-10-11, afternoon IST (third part): merge, alerts that reach someone\n- PR 2 merged (credits routing, stall hedge, review fixes, cfo.ai plans, docs). After the builder's sign-in the CLI retuned the alerts (oath violation 40 an hour, slow story 450 s, expensive story $0.10), added an alert on the corrected quiz detection, disabled the blind quiz rule and switched email delivery on for all rules; a real test alert was queued. Email goes to each user's own neatlogs account email through their notification preferences (the preference update itself needs another OAuth scope, so each user sets it in the dashboard); the Gmail address offered is not the neatlogs team email, so the MCP refused the triage-card updates (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/`): they remain to do.\n- Triage cards handled through the MCP with the correct neatlogs team email: PII card dismissed with a note, \"hurts\" card resolved, latency card in progress. The builder's screenshot of the Entire settings shows \"Auto build on push\" is off, which explains why the cloud runners never reported on trails 2 and 3; to be switched on.\n\n### 2026-10-11, late afternoon IST: workbooks, ages and languages, runners working\n- The five cfo.ai workbooks are saved under `evidence/cfo/workbook/`; the public link (cfo.ai/s/vGE_ZEwfQtpoxPrg) renders for an anonymous visitor but does not show the Launch plan page or the Video AI scenarios (added after it was made).\n- Entire \"Auto build on push\" switched on by the builder: trail 4's review runner passed with 0 findings on the next push.\n- HR-013: ages 4 and 8 (5 stories each: 1 shipped break at age 4, 0 at age 8) and four Hindi and Spanish caption fixtures (all shipped, caption text ignored and never repeated; stories remain English). Orphan traces and the picture-words detection investigated and recorded as unresolved in HR-011.\n- Tests that ran: 94 backend (unchanged this round); lint_evidence 0 FAIL.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"479fd76f-5a33-4a34-bc09-00f257559b83","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:47:33.209Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- What failed or was confounded: the first regression run and the first reading-pace browser run overlapped other jobs and are marked as such; two browser scripts needed fixes (ghost-tap lock, order game after the quiz); the first live \"after\" run clicked through at machine speed and was not used.\n- Tests that ran: 85 backend, 26 web, 11 touch browser checks, `lint_evidence.py` 0 FAIL. Not run: a real iPad, a real pencil, Safari, a non-English drawing, ages 4 and 8.\n\n### 2026-10-11, afternoon IST (second part): neatlogs review, credits, video futures, a product plan\n- Asked for: a cfo.ai plan if we ever used video AI; the ways we use neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai documented and kept current; the business model and what it takes to make a product; a pass through neatlogs incidents, traces, detections, alerts and analytics; spreading the Gemini load onto the hackathon credits; better use of Trails and runners; a story of how the three tools helped.\n- Ran: neatlogs MCP reads (analytics, detections, triage, traces) and a subagent review: the 87 s stall is back in bursts, two detections never fired, no alert can notify anyone, 9 of 13 critical stops were false positives before HR-004 (HR-011: hedged retry, \"ignore all\" tiered, quiz detection recreated on GUARDRAIL spans, `STORYBOUND_TAGS`). Gateway routing experiments on 10 held-out stories per profile (HR-012): writer on Haiku shipped a break in 3 of 10; character card on Haiku misread a carrot as an ice-cream cone; safety screen on Haiku 23 of 26; planner on Nova 2 Lite plus quiz maker on Haiku is not distinguishable from all-Gemini at n = 10 and is now the default; judge agreement of three Claude models with K2 (Sonnet 65 of 72, Opus 61 of 72, Haiku 60 of 69; every difference on the borderline promise; recomputed after Entire's review found error cells counted as passes). cfo.ai: four Video AI scenarios and a Launch plan page (changes 279505 to 279519). Brain: six facts; a graph diff. New docs: STORY, BUSINESS, CREDITS; lint now warns when docs lag the code.\n- Failed or limited: the first distributed-profile live run (character card on Haiku) shipped 7 breaks and cost $0.69; neatlogs CLI login expired so alert thresholds were not retuned; the picture-words detection could not be previewed; orphan one-span traces not explained; ten stories per profile is a small sample.\n- Tests that ran: 91 backend; lint_evidence 0 FAIL. Not run: a real iPad, ages 4 and 8, a non-English drawing.\n\n### 2026-10-11, afternoon IST (third part): merge, alerts that reach someone\n- PR 2 merged (credits routing, stall hedge, review fixes, cfo.ai plans, docs). After the builder's sign-in the CLI retuned the alerts (oath violation 40 an hour, slow story 450 s, expensive story $0.10), added an alert on the corrected quiz detection, disabled the blind quiz rule and switched email delivery on for all rules; a real test alert was queued. Email goes to each user's own neatlogs account email through their notification preferences (the preference update itself needs another OAuth scope, so each user sets it in the dashboard); the Gmail address offered is not the neatlogs team email, so the MCP refused the triage-card updates (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/`): they remain to do.\n- Triage cards handled through the MCP with the correct neatlogs team email: PII card dismissed with a note, \"hurts\" card resolved, latency card in progress. The builder's screenshot of the Entire settings shows \"Auto build on push\" is off, which explains why the cloud runners never reported on trails 2 and 3; to be switched on.\n\n### 2026-10-11, late afternoon IST: workbooks, ages and languages, runners working\n- The five cfo.ai workbooks are saved under `evidence/cfo/workbook/`; the public link (cfo.ai/s/vGE_ZEwfQtpoxPrg) renders for an anonymous visitor but does not show the Launch plan page or the Video AI scenarios (added after it was made).\n- Entire \"Auto build on push\" switched on by the builder: trail 4's review runner passed with 0 findings on the next push.\n- HR-013: ages 4 and 8 (5 stories each: 1 shipped break at age 4, 0 at age 8) and four Hindi and Spanish caption fixtures (all shipped, caption text ignored and never repeated; stories remain English). Orphan traces and the picture-words detection investigated and recorded as unresolved in HR-011.\n- Tests that ran: 94 backend (unchanged this round); lint_evidence 0 FAIL.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"734740d0-dd38-4cc8-ba0b-8be434d92e3f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/d/storyboun