{"parentUuid":"784ac5a2-c2ec-4139-96eb-42d784357716","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"93599b87-86af-4de1-a515-88e8eaaaeeca","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015JDEcm9WKFycGpZ9KAsioL","type":"tool_result","content":"17:## 1. neatlogs\n19:### Architecture\n25:### Implementation\n31:### Runtime: what the traces showed\n36:### Reasoning: how traces led to fixes\n50:### Result\n54:### What we tried that broke or did not work\n60:### Not done (and why)\n65:## 2. Entire\n67:### Architecture\n70:### Implementation\n77:### Runtime and reasoning\n80:### Trails (two trails; trail 2 is backed by a branch and a PR)\n86:### Result and limits (said plainly)\n94:## 3. cfo.ai\n96:### Architecture\n99:### Implementation\n104:### Runtime: what the model says (month 6, estimates)\n114:### Reasoning: the decision the model made\n117:### Result and limits\n127:## 4. The other tools, briefly\n132:## 5. Round two (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): what the evaluation guides, the launch question and the child's hands changed\n135:### neatlogs (measure the judge and the decisions, keep the traces)\n142:### Entire (rules that gate the next change)\n146:### cfo.ai (what a launch costs, beyond the model's three costs)\n149:### What the touch work added to the evidence\n154:## 6. Round three (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): reading the platforms back, and using the credits\n155:### neatlogs (a second pass through everything it holds)\n157:### Entire (decisions, memory and gates)\n159:### cfo.ai (video futures, a product plan, and the credits question)\n`web/scripts/e2e-touch.mjs` (11 behaviours through a touch-emulating browser) and 7 unit tests; screenshots in `evidence/screens/`. Entire's review runner has not yet seen them.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Round three (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): reading the platforms back, and using the credits\n### neatlogs (a second pass through everything it holds)\nThrough the MCP with the project key (reads need no login): analytics views (kpis, cost, errors, time, tools, detections, waste, workflows), the detection list and trends, the triage list, trace search and trace context. Result in [research/neatlogs-incident-review.md](research/neatlogs-incident-review.md) (a 135-line review by a subagent, checked against the ledger): 2,095 traces, 110 error trace\n### Entire (decisions, memory and gates)\nSix Brain facts recorded (`entire brain remember`): Veo only in `us-central1`; the gateway's budget and routes; the small-hands rules; the eval gate; the neatlogs login limit; tuning versus holdout. A graph diff of the picture-agent, touch-safety and early-painting commits is in `evidence/entire/20261011-1300-IST-graph-diff-auto-pictures-touch-early-painting.json`. That change (model routing, the \n### cfo.ai (video futures, a product plan, and the credits question)\nFour scenarios under Main for video AI (3 Lite clips; a clip on every page, Fast; 3 standard 8-second clips; a 3-minute animated story) with the video cost folded into the story cost formula (changes 279505 to 279515), and a new page \"Launch plan\" with the real operating cost, one-time launch cost, contribution per household, break-even households and the price that breaks even at 500 households (","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6ecc2afd-6c66-4d4e-832f-44fde576e311","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:47:39.852Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"17:## 1. neatlogs\n19:### Architecture\n25:### Implementation\n31:### Runtime: what the traces showed\n36:### Reasoning: how traces led to fixes\n50:### Result\n54:### What we tried that broke or did not work\n60:### Not done (and why)\n65:## 2. Entire\n67:### Architecture\n70:### Implementation\n77:### Runtime and reasoning\n80:### Trails (two trails; trail 2 is backed by a branch and a PR)\n86:### Result and limits (said plainly)\n94:## 3. cfo.ai\n96:### Architecture\n99:### Implementation\n104:### Runtime: what the model says (month 6, estimates)\n114:### Reasoning: the decision the model made\n117:### Result and limits\n127:## 4. The other tools, briefly\n132:## 5. Round two (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): what the evaluation guides, the launch question and the child's hands changed\n135:### neatlogs (measure the judge and the decisions, keep the traces)\n142:### Entire (rules that gate the next change)\n146:### cfo.ai (what a launch costs, beyond the model's three costs)\n149:### What the touch work added to the evidence\n154:## 6. Round three (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): reading the platforms back, and using the credits\n155:### neatlogs (a second pass through everything it holds)\n157:### Entire (decisions, memory and gates)\n159:### cfo.ai (video futures, a product plan, and the credits question)\n`web/scripts/e2e-touch.mjs` (11 behaviours through a touch-emulating browser) and 7 unit tests; screenshots in `evidence/screens/`. Entire's review runner has not yet seen them.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Round three (Sun 11 Oct, afternoon): reading the platforms back, and using the credits\n### neatlogs (a second pass through everything it holds)\nThrough the MCP with the project key (reads need no login): analytics views (kpis, cost, errors, time, tools, detections, waste, workflows), the detection list and trends, the triage list, trace search and trace context. Result in [research/neatlogs-incident-review.md](research/neatlogs-incident-review.md) (a 135-line review by a subagent, checked against the ledger): 2,095 traces, 110 error trace\n### Entire (decisions, memory and gates)\nSix Brain facts recorded (`entire brain remember`): Veo only in `us-central1`; the gateway's budget and routes; the small-hands rules; the eval gate; the neatlogs login limit; tuning versus holdout. A graph diff of the picture-agent, touch-safety and early-painting commits is in `evidence/entire/20261011-1300-IST-graph-diff-auto-pictures-touch-early-painting.json`. That change (model routing, the \n### cfo.ai (video futures, a product plan, and the credits question)\nFour scenarios under Main for video AI (3 Lite clips; a clip on every page, Fast; 3 standard 8-second clips; a 3-minute animated story) with the video cost folded into the story cost formula (changes 279505 to 279515), and a new page \"Launch plan\" with the real operating cost, one-time launch cost, contribution per household, break-even households and the price that breaks even at 500 households (","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8dafee5a-6fd3-4051-b0ec-383b082506a1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/d/storybound","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"784ac5a2-c2ec-4139-96eb-42d784357716","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
