rgin **[x]**, **[y]**, runway **[N]** months. The model chose the verification policy and the per-story budget, and those are fields in the oath config.\" |\n116:2. **Saturday night (first red trace):** \"Page 5 lost the hero's name. The check failed, the page was rewritten, the check passed. That's one trace. The oath caught it before the child could. #neatHack\" + the trace screenshot.\n133:<one-breath pitch>   <receipt screenshot>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d45bf2df-10d1-46da-a916-bfcfe63339cb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/d/storybound","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce2d48f1-3820-4e29-86cb-f6cbdf78aef0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"c47f5bd3-a933-4639-be8d-b537d9150ed3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14947270 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2ed08a17-8f6c-4717-af47-ec6e55af5a5b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:48:07.491Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14947270 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"2ed08a17-8f6c-4717-af47-ec6e55af5a5b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01MajAyijkwshhGURigSjLtt","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b9ce0ab4-1e75-4026-9197-7a0c5b48d842","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:48:27.055Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"b9ce0ab4-1e75-4026-9197-7a0c5b48d842","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyUmQKCa14j29Tiwbgu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wy8XnELsmKgLP9YCLybHDk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-SCRIPT.md","content":"# Demo video script (one video, at most 3:00)\n\nWritten for: the builder, who records and edits the video last. About 410 spoken words (about 2:50 at a calm pace); the screens are listed beside each line so each tool is shown on architecture, implementation, runtime, reasoning and result. Everything said here is backed by a file or trace in the repo; the pointer is in the right-hand column so nothing needs to be looked up while recording.\n\n**The three things the video must show (the brief):** the problem the agent solves · how cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project · how neatlogs was used to find and resolve the incidents the agent ran into.\n\n| Time | On screen | Say | Proof to have open |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0:00 to 0:20 | A child's crayon drawing of a bunny; the story's first page; a magnifier on one page with words painted into the picture | \"A child draws a bunny and asks for a story about sharing. A story model will write one. But nobody checks it: a word painted into the picture, a scary line, a lesson that never shows up. For a four to eight year old, that is the whole risk.\" | `assets/test-drawings/`, `evidence/stories/` |\n| 0:20 to 0:50 | The receipt screen: \"28 promises checked, 1 page rewritten, all kept\"; then a page failing a check and being rewritten | \"Storybound is an agent that writes an oath for each drawing and lesson, checks every page against it before the child sees it, rewrites any page that breaks it, and hands the parent a receipt. On the same writer, 27 of 28 stories shipped a broken promise without the checks. With them, none of 28.\" | [report](../evidence/reports/20261010-1505-IST-sweep-2-p2.md), [HR-008](../evidence/hardening/HR-008.md) |\n| 0:50 to 1:50 | neatlogs: one story trace, its GUARDRAIL spans with quotes; then the incident cards; then the three fixes side by side | **Architecture and implementation:** \"Every story is one neatlogs trace, and every promise is one span with the quoted words and the verdict. **Runtime:** we also broke things on purpose, so there would be incidents to find. **Incident one:** a stronger writer, Claude Sonnet, failed three stories in ten. In the trace the error span showed it had answered in a different shape. We made the parser accept both. Ten of ten. **Incident two:** with the judge down, no story shipped. Zero of five. We added a judge from another family. Five of five, and when both are down the child sees a try-again screen, never an unchecked story. **Incident three:** neatlogs opened its own cards, one said our repair loop never ends. We checked: the cap holds. The traces were fragments, because our worker threads lost their parent span. We fixed the tracing, and all four pictures and every picture check now sit inside the one story trace.\" | `evidence/hardening/HR-015.md`, `HR-016.md`, `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/triage_actions.json`, traces `640b8a6d6ed6cce8941ddab55139ffba` (after) and `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a` (before) |\n| 1:50 to 2:05 | The experiment table (writers, judge, no judge, no repairs) and the audit numbers | **Result:** \"We also asked whether a different design would beat ours. Without repairs, six of ten stories shipped a known break. Without the judge, 48 of 80 pages broke a promise nobody saw. A stronger writer halves the repairs at five times the cost, so the cheap writer plus repair stays.\" | `evidence/experiments/20261012-comparison.md`, [HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md) |\n| 2:05 to 2:30 | Entire: the checkpoint list, `entire why` on a line, the review findings, a trail with its runner passing | **Entire:** \"Entire kept every change as one intent with a checkpoint, so each fix above maps to one commit. Its review caught a real bug in our own evidence builder, and a missing fallback that would have turned a gateway outage into a failed story. Its trail runners now say what a prompt change must bring: a version bump, a hardening record, a regression run.\" | `evidence/entire/`, [TOOLS.md](TOOLS.md) section 2, [PR 1](https://github.com/hatif03/storybound/pull/1) |\n| 2:30 to 2:52 | cfo.ai: the Main scenario, margin cells, Version history of the cost edit, the video AI scenario in red | **cfo.ai:** \"cfo.ai turned 'what does a story cost' into a decision. Painting every page left a 43 percent margin; so the agent now spends a fixed picture budget on the pages that matter. We replaced its cost guess with the cost neatlogs measured. And it told us video AI would take the margin from 67 percent to minus 70, so motion stays a cheap, checked effect.\" | `evidence/cfo/`, [BUSINESS.md](BUSINESS.md), [HR-010](../evidence/hardening/HR-010.md) |\n| 2:52 to 3:00 | The receipt again, the repo name | \"Promises written, checked, repaired, and shown to a parent. Storybound.\" | n/a |\n\n## Recording notes\n- Show, do not tell, for the incidents: three screen captures, each under 15 s: the Sonnet error span (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/` and the X2 traces in the ledger), the drill C4 stopped runs next to C4b shipped, and the story trace before and after the span fix (span counts 2 of 4 pictures, 0 picture checks, against 4 and 8).\n- Every number is a small-sample result (ten stories per configuration, five per drill). Do not say \"always\" or \"proven\"; say what was measured. If time is short, cut the 1:50 to 2:05 block first.\n- No real child's face, name, school or location on screen; use the fixture bunny. The sister's drawings stay in `_private/`.\n- Name the tools on screen as you speak (a lower-third: neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai) so a judge scoring \"each tool covered on architecture, implementation, runtime, reasoning, result\" can tick the five.\n- If the human evaluation of judge verdicts has finished by recording time, add one sentence in the neatlogs block with its agreement number from `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/`; if not, say nothing about it.\n- After the video: put the link in `evidence/posts.md`, then the submission post (Mon 12 Oct, 19:00 to 23:55 IST).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1512,"cache_read_input_tokens":190427,"output_tokens":2300,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1512,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":190427,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1512},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Wy8XnELsmKgLP9YCLybHDk":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-SCRIPT.md","content":"# Demo video script (one video, at most 3:00)\n\nWritten for: the builder, who records and edits the video last. About 410 spoken words (about 2:50 at a calm pace); the screens are listed beside each line so each tool is shown on architecture, implementation, runtime, reasoning and result. Everything said here is backed by a file or trace in the repo; the pointer is in the right-hand column so nothing needs to be looked up while recording.\n\n**The three things the video must show (the brief):** the problem the agent solves · how cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project · how neatlogs was used to find and resolve the incidents the agent ran into.\n\n| Time | On screen | Say | Proof to have open |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0:00 to 0:20 | A child's crayon drawing of a bunny; the story's first page; a magnifier on one page with words painted into the picture | \"A child draws a bunny and asks for a story about sharing. A story model will write one. But nobody checks it: a word painted into the picture, a scary line, a lesson that never shows up. For a four to eight year old, that is the whole risk.\" | `assets/test-drawings/`, `evidence/stories/` |\n| 0:20 to 0:50 | The receipt screen: \"28 promises checked, 1 page rewritten, all kept\"; then a page failing a check and being rewritten | \"Storybound is an agent that writes an oath for each drawing and lesson, checks every page against it before the child sees it, rewrites any page that breaks it, and hands the parent a receipt. On the same writer, 27 of 28 stories shipped a broken promise without the checks. With them, none of 28.\" | [report](../evidence/reports/20261010-1505-IST-sweep-2-p2.md), [HR-008](../evidence/hardening/HR-008.md) |\n| 0:50 to 1:50 | neatlogs: one story trace, its GUARDRAIL spans with quotes; then the incident cards; then the three fixes side by side | **Architecture and implementation:** \"Every story is one neatlogs trace, and every promise is one span with the quoted words and the verdict. **Runtime:** we also broke things on purpose, so there would be incidents to find. **Incident one:** a stronger writer, Claude Sonnet, failed three stories in ten. In the trace the error span showed it had answered in a different shape. We made the parser accept both. Ten of ten. **Incident two:** with the judge down, no story shipped. Zero of five. We added a judge from another family. Five of five, and when both are down the child sees a try-again screen, never an unchecked story. **Incident three:** neatlogs opened its own cards, one said our repair loop never ends. We checked: the cap holds. The traces were fragments, because our worker threads lost their parent span. We fixed the tracing, and all four pictures and every picture check now sit inside the one story trace.\" | `evidence/hardening/HR-015.md`, `HR-016.md`, `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/triage_actions.json`, traces `640b8a6d6ed6cce8941ddab55139ffba` (after) and `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a` (before) |\n| 1:50 to 2:05 | The experiment table (writers, judge, no judge, no repairs) and the audit numbers | **Result:** \"We also asked whether a different design would beat ours. Without repairs, six of ten stories shipped a known break. Without the judge, 48 of 80 pages broke a promise nobody saw. A stronger writer halves the repairs at five times the cost, so the cheap writer plus repair stays.\" | `evidence/experiments/20261012-comparison.md`, [HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md) |\n| 2:05 to 2:30 | Entire: the checkpoint list, `entire why` on a line, the review findings, a trail with its runner passing | **Entire:** \"Entire kept every change as one intent with a checkpoint, so each fix above maps to one commit. Its review caught a real bug in our own evidence builder, and a missing fallback that would have turned a gateway outage into a failed story. Its trail runners now say what a prompt change must bring: a version bump, a hardening record, a regression run.\" | `evidence/entire/`, [TOOLS.md](TOOLS.md) section 2, [PR 1](https://github.com/hatif03/storybound/pull/1) |\n| 2:30 to 2:52 | cfo.ai: the Main scenario, margin cells, Version history of the cost edit, the video AI scenario in red | **cfo.ai:** \"cfo.ai turned 'what does a story cost' into a decision. Painting every page left a 43 percent margin; so the agent now spends a fixed picture budget on the pages that matter. We replaced its cost guess with the cost neatlogs measured. And it told us video AI would take the margin from 67 percent to minus 70, so motion stays a cheap, checked effect.\" | `evidence/cfo/`, [BUSINESS.md](BUSINESS.md), [HR-010](../evidence/hardening/HR-010.md) |\n| 2:52 to 3:00 | The receipt again, the repo name | \"Promises written, checked, repaired, and shown to a parent. Storybound.\" | n/a |\n\n## Recording notes\n- Show, do not tell, for the incidents: three screen captures, each under 15 s: the Sonnet error span (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/` and the X2 traces in the ledger), the drill C4 stopped runs next to C4b shipped, and the story trace before and after the span fix (span counts 2 of 4 pictures, 0 picture checks, against 4 and 8).\n- Every number is a small-sample result (ten stories per configuration, five per drill). Do not say \"always\" or \"proven\"; say what was measured. If time is short, cut the 1:50 to 2:05 block first.\n- No real child's face, name, school or location on screen; use the fixture bunny. The sister's drawings stay in `_private/`.\n- Name the tools on screen as you speak (a lower-third: neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai) so a judge scoring \"each tool covered on architecture, implementation, runtime, reasoning, result\" can tick the five.\n- If the human evaluation of judge verdicts has finished by recording time, add one sentence in the neatlogs block with its agreement number from `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/`; if not, say nothing about it.\n- After the video: put the link in `evidence/posts.md`, then the submission post (Mon 12 Oct, 19:00 to 23:55 IST).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"63d58eb1-343d-4cda-84ed-bc26d7700777","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwyUkwHzFYS3Jbs5BujM","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad48c0f2-0b35-43f9-9565-356b8607c887","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:48:27.054Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
