`, [HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md) |\n| 2:05 to 2:30 | Entire: the checkpoint list, `entire why` on a line, the review findings, a trail with its runner passing | **Entire:** \"Entire kept every change as one intent with a checkpoint, so each fix above maps to one commit. Its review caught a real bug in our own evidence builder, and a missing fallback that would have turned a gateway outage into a failed story. Its trail runners now say what a prompt change must bring: a version bump, a hardening record, a regression run.\" | `evidence/entire/`, [TOOLS.md](TOOLS.md) section 2, [PR 1](https://github.com/hatif03/storybound/pull/1) |\n| 2:30 to 2:52 | cfo.ai: the Main scenario, margin cells, Version history of the cost edit, the video AI scenario in red | **cfo.ai:** \"cfo.ai turned 'what does a story cost' into a decision. Painting every page left a 43 percent margin; so the agent now spends a fixed picture budget on the pages that matter. We replaced its cost guess with the cost neatlogs measured. And it told us video AI would take the margin from 67 percent to minus 70, so motion stays a cheap, checked effect.\" | `evidence/cfo/`, [BUSINESS.md](BUSINESS.md), [HR-010](../evidence/hardening/HR-010.md) |\n| 2:52 to 3:00 | The receipt again, the repo name | \"Promises written, checked, repaired, and shown to a parent. Storybound.\" | n/a |\n\n## Recording notes\n- Show, do not tell, for the incidents: three screen captures, each under 15 s: the Sonnet error span (`evidence/neatlogs/review-2/` and the X2 traces in the ledger), the drill C4 stopped runs next to C4b shipped, and the story trace before and after the span fix (span counts 2 of 4 pictures, 0 picture checks, against 4 and 8).\n- Every number is a small-sample result (ten stories per configuration, five per drill). Do not say \"always\" or \"proven\"; say what was measured. If time is short, cut the 1:50 to 2:05 block first.\n- No real child's face, name, school or location on screen; use the fixture bunny. The sister's drawings stay in `_private/`.\n- Name the tools on screen as you speak (a lower-third: neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai) so a judge scoring \"each tool covered on architecture, implementation, runtime, reasoning, result\" can tick the five.\n- If the human evaluation of judge verdicts has finished by recording time, add one sentence in the neatlogs block with its agreement number from `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/`; if not, say nothing about it.\n- After the video: put the link in `evidence/posts.md`, then the submission post (Mon 12 Oct, 19:00 to 23:55 IST).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad48c0f2-0b35-43f9-9565-356b8607c887","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
