{"parentUuid":"0767800b-c6ed-4180-9d1c-188a248ce667","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwzHSUbwJ7kj4deQFzeb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":220984,"output_tokens":1788,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":75},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1788,"cache_read_input_tokens":220984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":788,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"e5174614-344e-4c84-a6b0-3b7c100add63","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwzHS3Yvxq4xeguTSpDa","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4090ee29-305d-42b6-be22-d1df355ea2cc","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:58:42.516Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"4090ee29-305d-42b6-be22-d1df355ea2cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwzHSUbwJ7kj4deQFzeb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013vS5HgSKGorLnvoXZAXwPJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/TOOLS.md <<'E'\n\n---\n\n## 7. Round four (Mon 12 Oct): experiments, failure drills, incidents and a human check\n### neatlogs (incidents found, explained and resolved; one trace per story, whole)\n- **Experiments and drills as traces.** Eight configurations and eight injected failures ran as tagged sweeps (`experiment`, `chaos`), so the dashboard could be read like a lab notebook; the ledger carries the configuration beside each trace id ([HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md), [HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md)).\n- **Incidents it showed, and what we did.** The Claude Sonnet writer's three errors (opened in the error spans: a `choices` list where `correct` was expected) led to a tolerant parser and 10 of 10; the judge outage led to a failover judge from another family; a model outage shown as a refusal led to the try-again screen.\n- **Its own incident cards, checked before fixing.** Three new cards opened on 12 Oct. We opened each card's linked traces: the \"infinite repair loop\" card linked three-span fragments (a tracing fault of ours, not a loop: the repair cap holds); the `illustrate` latency card was our own image-429 drill, recovered as designed; the K2 \"prose\" card was refuted by the span (valid JSON only). All three were resolved with notes (`evidence/neatlogs/review-3/triage_actions.json`). The fragments led to [HR-016](../evidence/hardening/HR-016.md): worker threads now start from the workflow's context, and the story's span has an input and an output.\n- **Evaluations (human).** The first attempt added whole traces: the reviewer saw `{}` and `null`. It was closed and rebuilt as 17 single judge verdicts (3 violations, 14 passes), each opening on the promise, the page text and the verdict, with Agree / Disagree / Cannot tell and a reason; assigned to the builder. The result is the human-judge agreement, read from `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/` when answered; until then no agreement number is claimed.\n- **Detections.** \"Critical Violation Monitor\" and \"High Latency LLM Monitor\" were accepted from neatlogs's suggestions; the picture-words detection now has spans to read (its pattern matches a violation and not a pass; it has not fired because no picture had painted words).\n- **What cost time.** The CLI sign-in lasts about 15 minutes (we had assumed an hour), the trace export endpoint answered `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`, the evaluation form accepts `linear_scale` but rejected `rating`, and a multiple-choice question wants `options: {\"options\": [...]}`; the MCP helper kept working on the project key when the CLI login lapsed.\n\n### Entire (one commit per fix; the review of this branch)\nEach fix above is its own commit, so its checkpoint maps to one change (judge failover, tolerant parsing, the try-again screen, the span context, the story span's input and output). `entire review general` on PR 4 and the trail runner results are recorded in `evidence/entire/` (see the entry dated 12 Oct).\n\n### cfo.ai (what the experiments cost, as inputs)\nThe measured cost of the experiment writers and judges (a Gemini Pro writer $0.113 a story, a Sonnet writer $0.122, a second judge $0.138, against $0.024 for the default) is in [CREDITS.md](CREDITS.md); it supports keeping the cheap writer plus repair in the cfo.ai cost basis. The model itself was not changed this round.\nE\npython - <<'E'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('D:/storybound/docs/STORY.md'); s=f.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\nrow=\"| We broke it on purpose (12 Oct): eight configurations and eight injected failures, then read the dashboard like a lab notebook | A stronger writer's parse failure (3 of 10 stories) found in an error span and fixed (10 of 10); a judge outage (0 of 5 shipped) fixed by a judge from another family (5 of 5); three neatlogs incident cards checked: one revealed our own tracing fault (pictures and judge calls outside the story's trace, fixed: 4 of 4 pictures, no fragments), one was our drill, one was refuted by the span | [HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md), [HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md), [HR-016](../evidence/hardening/HR-016.md), `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/` |\\n\"\nanchor=\"| Two judge-family spans on the same page |\"\nassert anchor in s\nf.write_text(s.replace(anchor,row+anchor,1),encoding='utf-8')\nE\necho done","description":"Add round four to TOOLS and STORY"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":220984,"output_tokens":1788,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":75},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1788,"cache_read_input_tokens":220984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013vS5HgSKGorLnvoXZAXwPJ":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && cat >> docs/TOOLS.md <<'E'\n\n---\n\n## 7. Round four (Mon 12 Oct): experiments, failure drills, incidents and a human check\n### neatlogs (incidents found, explained and resolved; one trace per story, whole)\n- **Experiments and drills as traces.** Eight configurations and eight injected failures ran as tagged sweeps (`experiment`, `chaos`), so the dashboard could be read like a lab notebook; the ledger carries the configuration beside each trace id ([HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md), [HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md)).\n- **Incidents it showed, and what we did.** The Claude Sonnet writer's three errors (opened in the error spans: a `choices` list where `correct` was expected) led to a tolerant parser and 10 of 10; the judge outage led to a failover judge from another family; a model outage shown as a refusal led to the try-again screen.\n- **Its own incident cards, checked before fixing.** Three new cards opened on 12 Oct. We opened each card's linked traces: the \"infinite repair loop\" card linked three-span fragments (a tracing fault of ours, not a loop: the repair cap holds); the `illustrate` latency card was our own image-429 drill, recovered as designed; the K2 \"prose\" card was refuted by the span (valid JSON only). All three were resolved with notes (`evidence/neatlogs/review-3/triage_actions.json`). The fragments led to [HR-016](../evidence/hardening/HR-016.md): worker threads now start from the workflow's context, and the story's span has an input and an output.\n- **Evaluations (human).** The first attempt added whole traces: the reviewer saw `{}` and `null`. It was closed and rebuilt as 17 single judge verdicts (3 violations, 14 passes), each opening on the promise, the page text and the verdict, with Agree / Disagree / Cannot tell and a reason; assigned to the builder. The result is the human-judge agreement, read from `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/` when answered; until then no agreement number is claimed.\n- **Detections.** \"Critical Violation Monitor\" and \"High Latency LLM Monitor\" were accepted from neatlogs's suggestions; the picture-words detection now has spans to read (its pattern matches a violation and not a pass; it has not fired because no picture had painted words).\n- **What cost time.** The CLI sign-in lasts about 15 minutes (we had assumed an hour), the trace export endpoint answered `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`, the evaluation form accepts `linear_scale` but rejected `rating`, and a multiple-choice question wants `options: {\"options\": [...]}`; the MCP helper kept working on the project key when the CLI login lapsed.\n\n### Entire (one commit per fix; the review of this branch)\nEach fix above is its own commit, so its checkpoint maps to one change (judge failover, tolerant parsing, the try-again screen, the span context, the story span's input and output). `entire review general` on PR 4 and the trail runner results are recorded in `evidence/entire/` (see the entry dated 12 Oct).\n\n### cfo.ai (what the experiments cost, as inputs)\nThe measured cost of the experiment writers and judges (a Gemini Pro writer $0.113 a story, a Sonnet writer $0.122, a second judge $0.138, against $0.024 for the default) is in [CREDITS.md](CREDITS.md); it supports keeping the cheap writer plus repair in the cfo.ai cost basis. The model itself was not changed this round.\nE\npython - <<'E'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('D:/storybound/docs/STORY.md'); s=f.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\nrow=\"| We broke it on purpose (12 Oct): eight configurations and eight injected failures, then read the dashboard like a lab notebook | A stronger writer's parse failure (3 of 10 stories) found in an error span and fixed (10 of 10); a judge outage (0 of 5 shipped) fixed by a judge from another family (5 of 5); three neatlogs incident cards checked: one revealed our own tracing fault (pictures and judge calls outside the story's trace, fixed: 4 of 4 pictures, no fragments), one was our drill, one was refuted by the span | [HR-014](../evidence/hardening/HR-014.md), [HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md), [HR-016](../evidence/hardening/HR-016.md), `evidence/neatlogs/review-3/` |\\n\"\nanchor=\"| Two judge-family spans on the same page |\"\nassert anchor in s\nf.write_text(s.replace(anchor,row+anchor,1),encoding='utf-8')\nE\necho done","description":"Add round four to TOOLS and STORY"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_013vS5HgSKGorLnvoXZAXwPJ":{"cwd":"/d/storybound"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e5174614-344e-4c84-a6b0-3b7c100add63","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwzHS3Yvxq4xeguTSpDa","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d2094301-86c0-4f35-ab69-840a12741e8c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:58:54.504Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
