{"parentUuid":"59d961eb-111f-4670-b0a6-b3d03ccf4dcf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwzJXAQM46oYhHS7Lk1R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PvyGnTesxACoi3gXK7JKRE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> hackathon.md <<'E'\n\n### 2026-10-12, IST: experiments, failure drills, incidents, a human check, the span fix\n- Asked for: more incidents on the dashboard and a look at whether other configurations or architectures beat ours (neatlogs team), the evaluations the dashboard asked for, the orphan traces and the picture-words detection, a demo video script at the end.\n- Ran: eight configurations on ten held-out stories each plus an audit pass that re-judges shipped pages (HR-014), eight failure drills (HR-015), a diagnostic media run and a three-story clean run after the tracing fix (HR-016). Hypotheses were written in each HR record before the runs.\n- Found and fixed (one commit each): Sonnet writer page shape (3 of 10 errors, then 10 of 10), judge failover (0 of 5, then 5 of 5), outage shown as refusal, model error after retries shown as a generic error, worker threads outside the story's trace (2 of 4 pictures and all picture checks missing, then 4 of 4 and 8; one-span K2 traces about 9 a story, then none), the story span's empty input and output.\n- neatlogs: three new incident cards checked and resolved with notes (repair loop was fragments, `illustrate` latency was our drill, K2 \"prose\" refuted); an evaluation of whole traces was closed because reviewers saw `{}` and `null`, and rebuilt as 17 single judge verdicts for the builder to answer. The CLI login lasts about 15 minutes, so the evaluation work ran straight after each approval; trace export returned `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`.\n- Failed or limited: ten stories per configuration and five per drill; the audit judge is K2 itself; the picture-words detection has not fired (no picture had painted words); the C6 image-outage drill took 23 minutes per story (no picture time budget); the human agreement number does not exist until the builder answers the 17 verdicts.\n- Tests that ran: 101 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\nE\n.venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/build_evidence.py 2>&1 | tail -2; .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/lint_evidence.py 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Add build log entry, rebuild evidence index, lint","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1818,"cache_read_input_tokens":221906,"output_tokens":1014,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1818,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1014,"cache_read_input_tokens":221906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1818},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PvyGnTesxACoi3gXK7JKRE":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && cat >> hackathon.md <<'E'\n\n### 2026-10-12, IST: experiments, failure drills, incidents, a human check, the span fix\n- Asked for: more incidents on the dashboard and a look at whether other configurations or architectures beat ours (neatlogs team), the evaluations the dashboard asked for, the orphan traces and the picture-words detection, a demo video script at the end.\n- Ran: eight configurations on ten held-out stories each plus an audit pass that re-judges shipped pages (HR-014), eight failure drills (HR-015), a diagnostic media run and a three-story clean run after the tracing fix (HR-016). Hypotheses were written in each HR record before the runs.\n- Found and fixed (one commit each): Sonnet writer page shape (3 of 10 errors, then 10 of 10), judge failover (0 of 5, then 5 of 5), outage shown as refusal, model error after retries shown as a generic error, worker threads outside the story's trace (2 of 4 pictures and all picture checks missing, then 4 of 4 and 8; one-span K2 traces about 9 a story, then none), the story span's empty input and output.\n- neatlogs: three new incident cards checked and resolved with notes (repair loop was fragments, `illustrate` latency was our drill, K2 \"prose\" refuted); an evaluation of whole traces was closed because reviewers saw `{}` and `null`, and rebuilt as 17 single judge verdicts for the builder to answer. The CLI login lasts about 15 minutes, so the evaluation work ran straight after each approval; trace export returned `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`.\n- Failed or limited: ten stories per configuration and five per drill; the audit judge is K2 itself; the picture-words detection has not fired (no picture had painted words); the C6 image-outage drill took 23 minutes per story (no picture time budget); the human agreement number does not exist until the builder answers the 17 verdicts.\n- Tests that ran: 101 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\nE\n.venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/build_evidence.py 2>&1 | tail -2; .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/lint_evidence.py 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Add build log entry, rebuild evidence index, lint","timeout":120000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01PvyGnTesxACoi3gXK7JKRE":{"cwd":"/d/storybound"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"aca5671b-7c38-494e-8b47-900de9ac39aa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwzJWhd74HfEsqWkznK4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcf869fd-271e-4ea8-ad24-b0cdc432d0e7","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:59:04.155Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"extern