{"parentUuid":"ad977580-cd3f-4731-9de3-3b6b113a9cb9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99a95678-24d8-4442-985d-24006c95eea8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBetSzwjYfAtnz1YKycuGy","type":"tool_result","content":"50:    judge_ensemble: str = os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_JUDGE_ENSEMBLE\", \"\")  # a second judge from another family; the stricter verdict wins (experiment X3)\n61:    max_repair_attempts: int = int(os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_MAX_REPAIRS\", \"2\"))  # experiments X5 and X6 change it\n110:    hedge_after_s: float = float(os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_HEDGE_S\", \"45\"))  # HR-011: send a stalled text call a second time after this many seconds; 0 = off\n\"\"\"Failure injection for resilience drills. Off unless STORYBOUND_CHAOS is set; never set in the product.\n\nSTORYBOUND_CHAOS=\"target:kind:param:probability,...\" for example\n    gemini:stall:100:0.2      20% of Gemini calls first wait 100 s (the 87 s Vertex stall, made worse)\n    gemini:error:503:0.4      40% of Gemini calls fail with a 503\n    k2:error:503:1            the K2 judge is down\n    gateway:error:503:1       the hackathon gateway is down\n    image:error:429:0.8       80% of picture calls hit the quota\n\nTargets: gemini, k2, gateway, image, tts. Every injected failure is a real ClientError with the real retry rules, so the agent's own recovery\n(retry, hedge, fall back, degrade) is what is being tested. Drills are tagged in the ledger (`chaos`) and in neatlogs (`STORYBOUND_TAGS=chaos`).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport random\nimport time\n\nfrom .clients.errors import ClientError\n\n_RETRYABLE = {408, 429, 499, 500, 502, 503, 504}\n\n\ndef rules() -> list[tuple[str, str, float, float]]:\n    out = []\n    for part in os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_CHAOS\", \"\").split(\",\"):\n        bits = part.strip().split(\":\")\n        if len(bits) == 4:\n            try:\n                out.append((bits[0], bits[1], float(bits[2]), float(bits[3])))\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n    return out\n\n\ndef active() -> str:\n    return os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_CHAOS\", \"\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b9bef158-a337-4d5d-8aa7-d921e4e66bb8","timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:03:06.647Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"50:    judge_ensemble: str = os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_JUDGE_ENSEMBLE\", \"\")  # a second judge from another family; the stricter verdict wins (experiment X3)\n61:    max_repair_attempts: int = int(os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_MAX_REPAIRS\", \"2\"))  # experiments X5 and X6 change it\n110:    hedge_after_s: float = float(os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_HEDGE_S\", \"45\"))  # HR-011: send a stalled text call a second time after this many seconds; 0 = off\n\"\"\"Failure injection for resilience drills. Off unless STORYBOUND_CHAOS is set; never set in the product.\n\nSTORYBOUND_CHAOS=\"target:kind:param:probability,...\" for example\n    gemini:stall:100:0.2      20% of Gemini calls first wait 100 s (the 87 s Vertex stall, made worse)\n    gemini:error:503:0.4      40% of Gemini calls fail with a 503\n    k2:error:503:1            the K2 judge is down\n    gateway:error:503:1       the hackathon gateway is down\n    image:error:429:0.8       80% of picture calls hit the quota\n\nTargets: gemini, k2, gateway, image, tts. Every injected failure is a real ClientError with the real retry rules, so the agent's own recovery\n(retry, hedge, fall back, degrade) is what is being tested. Drills are tagged in the ledger (`chaos`) and in neatlogs (`STORYBOUND_TAGS=chaos`).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport random\nimport time\n\nfrom .clients.errors import ClientError\n\n_RETRYABLE = {408, 429, 499, 500, 502, 503, 504}\n\n\ndef rules() -> list[tuple[str, str, float, float]]:\n    out = []\n    for part in os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_CHAOS\", \"\").split(\",\"):\n        bits = part.strip().split(\":\")\n        if len(bits) == 4:\n            try:\n                out.append((bits[0], bits[1], float(bits[2]), float(bits[3])))\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n    return out\n\n\ndef active() -> str:\n    return os.environ.get(\"STORYBOUND_CHAOS\", \"\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dec04984-dfbf-4aec-a557-0324ea3ee13b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/d/storybound","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad977580-cd3f-4731-9de3-3b6b113a9cb9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
