{"parentUuid":"269e1b76-2b24-440e-bb27-936acd43b4bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwzhm3DfZHNitLcfMNU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CirajgsHpTgVqzhxD74i6L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > \"$TEMP/docs2.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef sub(p, pairs):\n    f = Path(p); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60])\n        s = s.replace(a, b)\n    f.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")\n\nsub(\"evidence/hardening/HR-015.md\", [(\"## Limits, said plainly\", '''## Found afterwards by Entire's review of this branch (`evidence/entire/20261012-IST-review-general-pr4.txt`)\n`entire review general` on the branch asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in the fixes above and are fixed, with tests:\n- **A refusal could become \"try again\":** every safety-screen failure was reported as an outage, including a provider's content block on a disturbing drawing. Now only a retryable service error is `screen_unavailable`; a block or an unreadable answer is `screen_inconclusive` and stays a refusal (fail closed).\n- **A pass could hide an unverified safety check:** in the second-judge ensemble one judge's pass overrode the other's `verification_error` on safety promises, and a `warning` tied with a `pass`. Safety promises now stay unverified if either judge could not run them, and the ranking has a place for `warning`.\n- **The failover paid the full retry time on every batch and wrote a fallback per call:** a judge that fails with a retryable error is skipped for a minute in that run, and the receipt lists the fallback once.\n- **A crash of a verifier counted as an outage:** the \"judges could not run\" stop now needs the judge's own \"unavailable\" error; a verifier crash or a quote-less violation stays a calm stop.\n- **Experiment settings in product code:** `STORYBOUND_MAX_REPAIRS` and `STORYBOUND_HEDGE_S` are parsed defensively, and every experiment setting that is set (repairs, ensemble, chaos, hedge) logs a warning at start.\n- **The page parser unwrapped any one-key answer:** only `page` and `scene` are unwrapped now.\n- **Tooling:** sweeps no longer force `pictures=auto` when no pictures are made (older sweeps stay comparable), the audit runs as one trace of its own and is metered, and the fragment counter skips a name that is not in the ledger.\nThe review also noted the fragment-trace counts are polluted by the audit's own traces (HR-016 already says so; the audit is now one trace).\n\n## Limits, said plainly'''),\n (\"## Regression fixture\\n\", \"## Regression fixture\\nThe review fixes: `tests/test_basics.py` (ensemble, failover, writer, settings) and `tests/test_pipeline.py` (screen outage against block).\\n\")\n])\nsub(\"docs/STATUS.md\", [(\"101 backend tests\", \"106 backend tests\")])\nsub(\"HANDOFF.md\", [(\"Tests: 101 backend\", \"Tests: 106 backend\")])\nsub(\"README.md\", [(\"101 backend\", \"106 backend\")])\nsub(\"hackathon.md\", [(\"- Tests that ran: 101 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\",\n \"- Entire's review of PR 4 asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in our own fixes (a refusal turned into \\\"try again\\\", a pass hiding an unverified safety check in the ensemble, a failover that re-paid its retries, a verifier crash counted as an outage, experiment settings unguarded, the parser unwrapping any key, sweep defaults) and are fixed with tests (HR-015, last section).\\n- Tests that ran: 106 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\")])\nsub(\"docs/TOOLS.md\", [(\"`entire review general` on PR 4 and the trail runner results are recorded in `evidence/entire/` (see the entry dated 12 Oct).\",\n \"`entire review general` on PR 4 (`evidence/entire/20261012-IST-review-general-pr4.txt`) asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in our own failure fixes, the most important being that the new try-again screen could replace a refusal of a drawing the safety screen had blocked, and that the second judge's pass could hide a safety check one judge could not run. All are fixed with tests ([HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md), last section).\")])\nPYEOF\npython \"$TEMP/docs2.py\" && .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/build_evidence.py | tail -1; .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/lint_evidence.py | tail -3","description":"Record the review fixes in docs and rebuild evidence","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":255264,"output_tokens":1816,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":111},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1816,"cache_read_input_tokens":255264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CirajgsHpTgVqzhxD74i6L":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && cat > \"$TEMP/docs2.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef sub(p, pairs):\n    f = Path(p); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60])\n        s = s.replace(a, b)\n    f.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")\n\nsub(\"evidence/hardening/HR-015.md\", [(\"## Limits, said plainly\", '''## Found afterwards by Entire's review of this branch (`evidence/entire/20261012-IST-review-general-pr4.txt`)\n`entire review general` on the branch asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in the fixes above and are fixed, with tests:\n- **A refusal could become \"try again\":** every safety-screen failure was reported as an outage, including a provider's content block on a disturbing drawing. Now only a retryable service error is `screen_unavailable`; a block or an unreadable answer is `screen_inconclusive` and stays a refusal (fail closed).\n- **A pass could hide an unverified safety check:** in the second-judge ensemble one judge's pass overrode the other's `verification_error` on safety promises, and a `warning` tied with a `pass`. Safety promises now stay unverified if either judge could not run them, and the ranking has a place for `warning`.\n- **The failover paid the full retry time on every batch and wrote a fallback per call:** a judge that fails with a retryable error is skipped for a minute in that run, and the receipt lists the fallback once.\n- **A crash of a verifier counted as an outage:** the \"judges could not run\" stop now needs the judge's own \"unavailable\" error; a verifier crash or a quote-less violation stays a calm stop.\n- **Experiment settings in product code:** `STORYBOUND_MAX_REPAIRS` and `STORYBOUND_HEDGE_S` are parsed defensively, and every experiment setting that is set (repairs, ensemble, chaos, hedge) logs a warning at start.\n- **The page parser unwrapped any one-key answer:** only `page` and `scene` are unwrapped now.\n- **Tooling:** sweeps no longer force `pictures=auto` when no pictures are made (older sweeps stay comparable), the audit runs as one trace of its own and is metered, and the fragment counter skips a name that is not in the ledger.\nThe review also noted the fragment-trace counts are polluted by the audit's own traces (HR-016 already says so; the audit is now one trace).\n\n## Limits, said plainly'''),\n (\"## Regression fixture\\n\", \"## Regression fixture\\nThe review fixes: `tests/test_basics.py` (ensemble, failover, writer, settings) and `tests/test_pipeline.py` (screen outage against block).\\n\")\n])\nsub(\"docs/STATUS.md\", [(\"101 backend tests\", \"106 backend tests\")])\nsub(\"HANDOFF.md\", [(\"Tests: 101 backend\", \"Tests: 106 backend\")])\nsub(\"README.md\", [(\"101 backend\", \"106 backend\")])\nsub(\"hackathon.md\", [(\"- Tests that ran: 101 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\",\n \"- Entire's review of PR 4 asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in our own fixes (a refusal turned into \\\"try again\\\", a pass hiding an unverified safety check in the ensemble, a failover that re-paid its retries, a verifier crash counted as an outage, experiment settings unguarded, the parser unwrapping any key, sweep defaults) and are fixed with tests (HR-015, last section).\\n- Tests that ran: 106 backend (pytest), ruff clean. Not run: the web tests this round (no web code changed).\")])\nsub(\"docs/TOOLS.md\", [(\"`entire review general` on PR 4 and the trail runner results are recorded in `evidence/entire/` (see the entry dated 12 Oct).\",\n \"`entire review general` on PR 4 (`evidence/entire/20261012-IST-review-general-pr4.txt`) asked for changes on ten points; seven were real defects in our own failure fixes, the most important being that the new try-again screen could replace a refusal of a drawing the safety screen had blocked, and that the second judge's pass could hide a safety check one judge could not run. All are fixed with tests ([HR-015](../evidence/hardening/HR-015.md), last section).\")])\nPYEOF\npython \"$TEMP/docs2.py\" && .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/build_evidence.py | tail -1; .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/lint_evidence.py | tail -3","description":"Record the review fixes in docs and rebuild evidence","timeout":120000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01CirajgsHpTgVqzhxD74i6L":{"cwd":"/d/storybound"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9d498407-744d-4c1b-83e9-db5377f99aa1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfwz