{"parentUuid":"602b404e-caac-4360-b867-319894aa6e9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfx1sHQhTcu41XgoyNPGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HUvuf2mVcot2SXjf1qwZ2k","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md","content":"# Recording guide: our app, neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai\n\nWritten for: the builder, who records the one demo video (at most 3:00, script in [DEMO-SCRIPT.md](DEMO-SCRIPT.md)). Four captures, each short; the script says which seconds of each to use.\n\n**Who records what.** The app capture is already made by a script (below), so you only need to record the three dashboards. The dashboards are behind your own logins (neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai); a script should not sign in as you, so you record them with OBS (it is in your taskbar) or Windows Game Bar (`Win + Alt + R`).\n\n**Before you press record (all captures)**\n- 1920 x 1080, browser zoom 100%, dark or light but the same for all three dashboards; close the bookmarks bar and other tabs.\n- Hide what must not show: your email address (neatlogs, cfo.ai, Entire account menus), API keys, the `.env` file, `_private/`, any child's name. Do not open settings pages with keys.\n- Move the mouse slowly, and pause one second on each thing you want a viewer to read. Record each segment as its own clip; do not try to do it in one take.\n- Rehearse the clicks once without recording.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Our app (made for you)\nFile: `evidence/demo/app-walkthrough.webm` (a real story, real models, no mock; about 12 minutes raw because the story is really made while the recording runs). Cut it to about 45 seconds for the video: speed up the waiting with a 10x speed ramp, keep these moments at normal speed.\n\nWhat the recording shows, in order, and what to say:\n| Moment | What is on screen | What to say |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome, \"Let's go\" | The home screen | \"A child draws their own hero.\" |\n| Drawing | A bunny drawn with the mouse | \"No photo upload needed; this is drawn on the screen.\" |\n| Name, lesson | Pip picks a name; the lesson card \"Sharing\"; the grown-up promise box with \"Nobody in the story is left out\" | \"A parent chooses the lesson and can add a promise of their own.\" |\n| Making the first page | The waiting screen | \"Behind this screen the agent wrote an oath and is checking each page against it.\" |\n| Reading a page | A picture, the scene, two choices | \"Every page was checked before the child sees it.\" |\n| A wrong answer | The story line shown after a wrong choice | \"A wrong answer teaches, never scolds.\" |\n| The quiz and the picture-order game | Four questions; the order game | \"The quiz questions are verified too; a question that fails a promise is dropped.\" |\n| Grown-ups, the receipt tab | The sum gate, the receipt: promises checked, pages rewritten, \"could not be fully kept\" | **This is the most important frame.** \"The parent gets a receipt: how many promises were checked, how many pages were rewritten, and which could not be kept.\" |\n| Forget | The story deleted | \"And a parent can make the app forget the story.\" |\n\nTo run it again (costs about $0.45): start the server (`.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m uvicorn storybound.api:app --app-dir src --port 8000`), then `cd web; node scripts\\e2e-real.mjs --no-video --pictures auto --dwell 4 --record ..\\evidence\\demo\\app-walkthrough.webm`. Add `--pictures full` to paint every page. To drive it by hand: open http://127.0.0.1:8000, press \"Let's go\", draw with the mouse or a finger (a simple shape is fine), \"Done!\", pick a name, pick \"Sharing\", press \"Yes!\", then read and answer; the grown-ups area is the small button on the top corner (answer the multiplication to open it).\n\n## 2. neatlogs dashboard (about 60 seconds in the video, the longest block)\nOpen https://app.neatlogs.com, project \"Mohammad's project\". Record these in order:\n1. **Traces** list, filter workflow `create-storybook`. Open `640b8a6d6ed6cce8941ddab55139ffba` (a story after the tracing fix). Expand the tree: the `node.*` steps, then a `verify:...` GUARDRAIL span; click it and show the quoted text, the verdict, the judge model. Say: \"every promise is one span with the words it relied on.\"\n2. **Before and after the tracing fix.** Show the trace `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a` (208 spans, two pictures) then `640b8a6d...` (225 spans, four pictures and eight picture checks). Use the span counts shown at the top of each trace. (If the dashboard has dropped the old trace, use [the saved span lists](../evidence/traces/) on screen instead.)\n3. **Incidents** page: the three cards that opened on 12 Oct, each resolved with a note: \"Resolve Infinite Repair Loop...\" (our tracing fault, not a loop), \"Investigate Latency and Quota Exhaustion in `illustrate`\" (our own drill), \"Enforce Structured JSON Outputs ... K2\" (refuted by the span). Open the first one, scroll to its resolution note and its linked traces (the three-span fragments). Say what the incident feature did: it surfaced fragments that led to the tracing fix.\n4. **A failure we caused and fixed:** search traces by tag `chaos`; show a stopped story from drill C4 (judge down, `1efb456ec688b4562947eb2f47cafaff`) next to a shipped one from C4b (`308ba676b437e79ba455a82b7f853d54` is the C3b error; use any C4b trace from the ledger). Say: \"zero of five before the failover, five of five after.\"\n5. **Detections** page: \"Picture has words painted in\" with its hits (after the picture-words drill, trace `c2a67d3482bbdff5beb6df58a4daf92b`), \"Oath violation\", \"Critical Violation Monitor\".\n6. **Alerts** (email delivery on) and **Evals**: the evaluation \"Do you agree with this verdict?\" with your answers, if you have given them. Say the agreement number only if the dashboard shows one.\n7. **Analytics**: cost per story and latency, one screen.\n\n## 3. Entire dashboard (about 25 seconds)\nOpen https://entire.io/gh/hatif03/storybound.\n1. The **commits / checkpoints** list: each commit with its checkpoint. Click the checkpoint of a fix, for example the commit \"Start judge calls and pictures from the workflow's context ...\", and show the session transcript summary. Say: \"one fix, one commit, one checkpoint.\"\n2. **Trails**: the open trail for this branch (PR 4), its **runner results** (review and gates), and the PR's **review findings** (the ten points from `entire review general`; seven were real defects in our own fixes). Show one finding next to the commit that fixed it.\n3. A terminal clip (15 seconds): `entire why src/storybound/oath/judge.py` and `entire brain recall \"judge\"` to show Brain facts. (Run them in the repo; they print file and checkpoint links.)\n\n## 4. cfo.ai (about 25 seconds)\nOpen the shared model at https://app.cfo.ai (workspace \"invisible-technologies\").\n1. **Unit economics** page, Main scenario: 77% gross margin for the Household plan at month 6.\n2. **Verification and illustration policy**: \"Verify all plus half the pictures: 67.8%; all eight pictures: 43.4%\". Say: \"this is the number that made the agent choose which pages to paint.\"\n3. Open **Version history** (the clock icon) and point at \"Edited cell `Cost input` = Text and verification B1 gated for Cost input basis\": the cost estimate replaced by the neatlogs measurement. The two screenshots are saved: [Unit economics](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1332-IST-cfo-version-history-unit-economics.png) and [Verification policy](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1333-IST-cfo-version-history-verification-policy.png).\n4. **Launch plan** and the **Video AI** scenario (margin to minus 70%). One second each.\n\n---\n\n## How the captures fit the three questions the video must answer\n- **The problem the agent solves:** capture 1 (the receipt frame).\n- **How cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project:** captures 4 and 3.\n- **How neatlogs found and resolved the incidents:** capture 2, items 2, 3 and 4 (the three incidents, shown as before and after).\n\n## Safety checks before you export\nPlay the final file once with the sound off and look for: an email address, a key, a repository secret, a surname, a child's face. The app capture uses a drawn bunny only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":295737,"output_tokens":3209,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3209,"cache_read_input_tokens":295737,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HUvuf2mVcot2SXjf1qwZ2k":{"file_path":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md","content":"# Recording guide: our app, neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai\n\nWritten for: the builder, who records the one demo video (at most 3:00, script in [DEMO-SCRIPT.md](DEMO-SCRIPT.md)). Four captures, each short; the script says which seconds of each to use.\n\n**Who records what.** The app capture is already made by a script (below), so you only need to record the three dashboards. The dashboards are behind your own logins (neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai); a script should not sign in as you, so you record them with OBS (it is in your taskbar) or Windows Game Bar (`Win + Alt + R`).\n\n**Before you press record (all captures)**\n- 1920 x 1080, browser zoom 100%, dark or light but the same for all three dashboards; close the bookmarks bar and other tabs.\n- Hide what must not show: your email address (neatlogs, cfo.ai, Entire account menus), API keys, the `.env` file, `_private/`, any child's name. Do not open settings pages with keys.\n- Move the mouse slowly, and pause one second on each thing you want a viewer to read. Record each segment as its own clip; do not try to do it in one take.\n- Rehearse the clicks once without recording.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Our app (made for you)\nFile: `evidence/demo/app-walkthrough.webm` (a real story, real models, no mock; about 12 minutes raw because the story is really made while the recording runs). Cut it to about 45 seconds for the video: speed up the waiting with a 10x speed ramp, keep these moments at normal speed.\n\nWhat the recording shows, in order, and what to say:\n| Moment | What is on screen | What to say |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome, \"Let's go\" | The home screen | \"A child draws their own hero.\" |\n| Drawing | A bunny drawn with the mouse | \"No photo upload needed; this is drawn on the screen.\" |\n| Name, lesson | Pip picks a name; the lesson card \"Sharing\"; the grown-up promise box with \"Nobody in the story is left out\" | \"A parent chooses the lesson and can add a promise of their own.\" |\n| Making the first page | The waiting screen | \"Behind this screen the agent wrote an oath and is checking each page against it.\" |\n| Reading a page | A picture, the scene, two choices | \"Every page was checked before the child sees it.\" |\n| A wrong answer | The story line shown after a wrong choice | \"A wrong answer teaches, never scolds.\" |\n| The quiz and the picture-order game | Four questions; the order game | \"The quiz questions are verified too; a question that fails a promise is dropped.\" |\n| Grown-ups, the receipt tab | The sum gate, the receipt: promises checked, pages rewritten, \"could not be fully kept\" | **This is the most important frame.** \"The parent gets a receipt: how many promises were checked, how many pages were rewritten, and which could not be kept.\" |\n| Forget | The story deleted | \"And a parent can make the app forget the story.\" |\n\nTo run it again (costs about $0.45): start the server (`.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m uvicorn storybound.api:app --app-dir src --port 8000`), then `cd web; node scripts\\e2e-real.mjs --no-video --pictures auto --dwell 4 --record ..\\evidence\\demo\\app-walkthrough.webm`. Add `--pictures full` to paint every page. To drive it by hand: open http://127.0.0.1:8000, press \"Let's go\", draw with the mouse or a finger (a simple shape is fine), \"Done!\", pick a name, pick \"Sharing\", press \"Yes!\", then read and answer; the grown-ups area is the small button on the top corner (answer the multiplication to open it).\n\n## 2. neatlogs dashboard (about 60 seconds in the video, the longest block)\nOpen https://app.neatlogs.com, project \"Mohammad's project\". Record these in order:\n1. **Traces** list, filter workflow `create-storybook`. Open `640b8a6d6ed6cce8941ddab55139ffba` (a story after the tracing fix). Expand the tree: the `node.*` steps, then a `verify:...` GUARDRAIL span; click it and show the quoted text, the verdict, the judge model. Say: \"every promise is one span with the words it relied on.\"\n2. **Before and after the tracing fix.** Show the trace `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a` (208 spans, two pictures) then `640b8a6d...` (225 spans, four pictures and eight picture checks). Use the span counts shown at the top of each trace. (If the dashboard has dropped the old trace, use [the saved span lists](../evidence/traces/) on screen instead.)\n3. **Incidents** page: the three cards that opened on 12 Oct, each resolved with a note: \"Resolve Infinite Repair Loop...\" (our tracing fault, not a loop), \"Investigate Latency and Quota Exhaustion in `illustrate`\" (our own drill), \"Enforce Structured JSON Outputs ... K2\" (refuted by the span). Open the first one, scroll to its resolution note and its linked traces (the three-span fragments). Say what the incident feature did: it surfaced fragments that led to the tracing fix.\n4. **A failure we caused and fixed:** search traces by tag `chaos`; show a stopped story from drill C4 (judge down, `1efb456ec688b4562947eb2f47cafaff`) next to a shipped one from C4b (`308ba676b437e79ba455a82b7f853d54` is the C3b error; use any C4b trace from the ledger). Say: \"zero of five before the failover, five of five after.\"\n5. **Detections** page: \"Picture has words painted in\" with its hits (after the picture-words drill, trace `c2a67d3482bbdff5beb6df58a4daf92b`), \"Oath violation\", \"Critical Violation Monitor\".\n6. **Alerts** (email delivery on) and **Evals**: the evaluation \"Do you agree with this verdict?\" with your answers, if you have given them. Say the agreement number only if the dashboard shows one.\n7. **Analytics**: cost per story and latency, one screen.\n\n## 3. Entire dashboard (about 25 seconds)\nOpen https://entire.io/gh/hatif03/storybound.\n1. The **commits / checkpoints** list: each commit with its checkpoint. Click the checkpoint of a fix, for example the commit \"Start judge calls and pictures from the workflow's context ...\", and show the session transcript summary. Say: \"one fix, one commit, one checkpoint.\"\n2. **Trails**: the open trail for this branch (PR 4), its **runner results** (review and gates), and the PR's **review findings** (the ten points from `entire review general`; seven were real defects in our own fixes). Show one finding next to the commit that fixed it.\n3. A terminal clip (15 seconds): `entire why src/storybound/oath/judge.py` and `entire brain recall \"judge\"` to show Brain facts. (Run them in the repo; they print file and checkpoint links.)\n\n## 4. cfo.ai (about 25 seconds)\nOpen the shared model at https://app.cfo.ai (workspace \"invisible-technologies\").\n1. **Unit economics** page, Main scenario: 77% gross margin for the Household plan at month 6.\n2. **Verification and illustration policy**: \"Verify all plus half the pictures: 67.8%; all eight pictures: 43.4%\". Say: \"this is the number that made the agent choose which pages to paint.\"\n3. Open **Version history** (the clock icon) and point at \"Edited cell `Cost input` = Text and verification B1 gated for Cost input basis\": the cost estimate replaced by the neatlogs measurement. The two screenshots are saved: [Unit economics](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1332-IST-cfo-version-history-unit-economics.png) and [Verification policy](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1333-IST-cfo-version-history-verification-policy.png).\n4. **Launch plan** and the **Video AI** scenario (margin to minus 70%). One second each.\n\n---\n\n## How the captures fit the three questions the video must answer\n- **The problem the agent solves:** capture 1 (the receipt frame).\n- **How cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project:** captures 4 and 3.\n- **How neatlogs found and resolved the incidents:** capture 2, items 2, 3 and 4 (the three incidents, shown as before and after).\n\n## Safety checks before you export\nPlay the final file once with the sound off and look for: an email address, a key, a repository secret, a surname, a child's face. The app capture uses a drawn bunny only.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8f1e2927-a244-4ab8-a2d6-dc8c5319272e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfx1sGgJPh3VmsxPC1pks","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b66ed30-2f98-4617-9e26-ed31182e46c5","timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:19:53.103Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"3b66ed30-2f98-4617-9e26-ed31182e46c5","snapshotMessageId":"ad327909-e2d5-4f05-a5b0-1ab34f3f5ff1","trackingPath":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-12T08:19:53.269Z","realParentDir":"D:\\storybound\\docs"},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:19:53.273Z"}
{"parentUuid":"3b66ed30-2f98-4617-9e26-ed31182e46c5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"99a95678-24d8-4442-985d-24006c95eea8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUvuf2mVcot2SXjf1qwZ2k","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"c58efcf7-3ee1-4328-8245-9275eebf51dd","timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:19:54.324Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"D:\\storybound\\docs\\DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md","content":"# Recording guide: our app, neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai\n\nWritten for: the builder, who records the one demo video (at most 3:00, script in [DEMO-SCRIPT.md](DEMO-SCRIPT.md)). Four captures, each short; the script says which seconds of each to use.\n\n**Who records what.** The app capture is already made by a script (below), so you only need to record the three dashboards. The dashboards are behind your own logins (neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai); a script should not sign in as you, so you record them with OBS (it is in your taskbar) or Windows Game Bar (`Win + Alt + R`).\n\n**Before you press record (all captures)**\n- 1920 x 1080, browser zoom 100%, dark or light but the same for all three dashboards; close the bookmarks bar and other tabs.\n- Hide what must not show: your email address (neatlogs, cfo.ai, Entire account menus), API keys, the `.env` file, `_private/`, any child's name. Do not open settings pages with keys.\n- Move the mouse slowly, and pause one second on each thing you want a viewer to read. Record each segment as its own clip; do not try to do it in one take.\n- Rehearse the clicks once without recording.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Our app (made for you)\nFile: `evidence/demo/app-walkthrough.webm` (a real story, real models, no mock; about 12 minutes raw because the story is really made while the recording runs). Cut it to about 45 seconds for the video: speed up the waiting with a 10x speed ramp, keep these moments at normal speed.\n\nWhat the recording shows, in order, and what to say:\n| Moment | What is on screen | What to say |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome, \"Let's go\" | The home screen | \"A child draws their own hero.\" |\n| Drawing | A bunny drawn with the mouse | \"No photo upload needed; this is drawn on the screen.\" |\n| Name, lesson | Pip picks a name; the lesson card \"Sharing\"; the grown-up promise box with \"Nobody in the story is left out\" | \"A parent chooses the lesson and can add a promise of their own.\" |\n| Making the first page | The waiting screen | \"Behind this screen the agent wrote an oath and is checking each page against it.\" |\n| Reading a page | A picture, the scene, two choices | \"Every page was checked before the child sees it.\" |\n| A wrong answer | The story line shown after a wrong choice | \"A wrong answer teaches, never scolds.\" |\n| The quiz and the picture-order game | Four questions; the order game | \"The quiz questions are verified too; a question that fails a promise is dropped.\" |\n| Grown-ups, the receipt tab | The sum gate, the receipt: promises checked, pages rewritten, \"could not be fully kept\" | **This is the most important frame.** \"The parent gets a receipt: how many promises were checked, how many pages were rewritten, and which could not be kept.\" |\n| Forget | The story deleted | \"And a parent can make the app forget the story.\" |\n\nTo run it again (costs about $0.45): start the server (`.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m uvicorn storybound.api:app --app-dir src --port 8000`), then `cd web; node scripts\\e2e-real.mjs --no-video --pictures auto --dwell 4 --record ..\\evidence\\demo\\app-walkthrough.webm`. Add `--pictures full` to paint every page. To drive it by hand: open http://127.0.0.1:8000, press \"Let's go\", draw with the mouse or a finger (a simple shape is fine), \"Done!\", pick a name, pick \"Sharing\", press \"Yes!\", then read and answer; the grown-ups area is the small button on the top corner (answer the multiplication to open it).\n\n## 2. neatlogs dashboard (about 60 seconds in the video, the longest block)\nOpen https://app.neatlogs.com, project \"Mohammad's project\". Record these in order:\n1. **Traces** list, filter workflow `create-storybook`. Open `640b8a6d6ed6cce8941ddab55139ffba` (a story after the tracing fix). Expand the tree: the `node.*` steps, then a `verify:...` GUARDRAIL span; click it and show the quoted text, the verdict, the judge model. Say: \"every promise is one span with the words it relied on.\"\n2. **Before and after the tracing fix.** Show the trace `f238415f0de63afe58fcbf9a32ff4f2a` (208 spans, two pictures) then `640b8a6d...` (225 spans, four pictures and eight picture checks). Use the span counts shown at the top of each trace. (If the dashboard has dropped the old trace, use [the saved span lists](../evidence/traces/) on screen instead.)\n3. **Incidents** page: the three cards that opened on 12 Oct, each resolved with a note: \"Resolve Infinite Repair Loop...\" (our tracing fault, not a loop), \"Investigate Latency and Quota Exhaustion in `illustrate`\" (our own drill), \"Enforce Structured JSON Outputs ... K2\" (refuted by the span). Open the first one, scroll to its resolution note and its linked traces (the three-span fragments). Say what the incident feature did: it surfaced fragments that led to the tracing fix.\n4. **A failure we caused and fixed:** search traces by tag `chaos`; show a stopped story from drill C4 (judge down, `1efb456ec688b4562947eb2f47cafaff`) next to a shipped one from C4b (`308ba676b437e79ba455a82b7f853d54` is the C3b error; use any C4b trace from the ledger). Say: \"zero of five before the failover, five of five after.\"\n5. **Detections** page: \"Picture has words painted in\" with its hits (after the picture-words drill, trace `c2a67d3482bbdff5beb6df58a4daf92b`), \"Oath violation\", \"Critical Violation Monitor\".\n6. **Alerts** (email delivery on) and **Evals**: the evaluation \"Do you agree with this verdict?\" with your answers, if you have given them. Say the agreement number only if the dashboard shows one.\n7. **Analytics**: cost per story and latency, one screen.\n\n## 3. Entire dashboard (about 25 seconds)\nOpen https://entire.io/gh/hatif03/storybound.\n1. The **commits / checkpoints** list: each commit with its checkpoint. Click the checkpoint of a fix, for example the commit \"Start judge calls and pictures from the workflow's context ...\", and show the session transcript summary. Say: \"one fix, one commit, one checkpoint.\"\n2. **Trails**: the open trail for this branch (PR 4), its **runner results** (review and gates), and the PR's **review findings** (the ten points from `entire review general`; seven were real defects in our own fixes). Show one finding next to the commit that fixed it.\n3. A terminal clip (15 seconds): `entire why src/storybound/oath/judge.py` and `entire brain recall \"judge\"` to show Brain facts. (Run them in the repo; they print file and checkpoint links.)\n\n## 4. cfo.ai (about 25 seconds)\nOpen the shared model at https://app.cfo.ai (workspace \"invisible-technologies\").\n1. **Unit economics** page, Main scenario: 77% gross margin for the Household plan at month 6.\n2. **Verification and illustration policy**: \"Verify all plus half the pictures: 67.8%; all eight pictures: 43.4%\". Say: \"this is the number that made the agent choose which pages to paint.\"\n3. Open **Version history** (the clock icon) and point at \"Edited cell `Cost input` = Text and verification B1 gated for Cost input basis\": the cost estimate replaced by the neatlogs measurement. The two screenshots are saved: [Unit economics](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1332-IST-cfo-version-history-unit-economics.png) and [Verification policy](../evidence/cfo/20261012-1333-IST-cfo-version-history-verification-policy.png).\n4. **Launch plan** and the **Video AI** scenario (margin to minus 70%). One second each.\n\n---\n\n## How the captures fit the three questions the video must answer\n- **The problem the agent solves:** capture 1 (the receipt frame).\n- **How cfo.ai and Entire were part of the project:** captures 4 and 3.\n- **How neatlogs found and resolved the incidents:** capture 2, items 2, 3 and 4 (the three incidents, shown as before and after).\n\n## Safety checks before you export\nPlay the final file once with the sound off and look for: an email address, a key, a repository secret, a surname, a child's face. The app capture uses a drawn bunny only.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b66ed30-2f98-4617-9e26-ed31182e46c5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
