{"parentUuid":"dae64b13-d4a6-44c9-a709-e7a1bf902b5f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfx2nnLjPrJjF7wD2uoAm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019D9V1a5z1Pn2Jcd8BGqVNa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > \"$TEMP/hr16b.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef sub(p, pairs):\n    f = Path(p); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60])\n        s = s.replace(a, b, 1)\n    f.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")\n\nsub(\"evidence/hardening/HR-016.md\", [\n (\"the verdict spans exist; its pattern matches a violation verdict and not a pass; **no story in these runs had a picture with words, so it has not fired** |\",\n  \"**fired**: on the picture-words drill (below) neatlogs counted 1 occurrence on 12 Oct ([trend](../traces/20261012-1401-IST-detection-trend-picture-words-after-drill.json)); before the drill it had 0 over seven days |\"),\n (\"- The detection is correct on the span format but unproven on a real violation; a picture with painted words would have to occur (the vision judge flagged none in these runs).\\n\",\n  \"- The detection fired on a picture we made (below), not on one the painter produced unprompted by us; in that run the real painter's pictures for two other pages were also flagged by the vision judge (Claude Haiku), and we have not checked by eye whether those were true words or judge errors.\\n\"),\n (\"## Limits, said plainly\", '''## The picture-words drill (the detection, tested end to end)\n`scripts/drill_picture_words.py` replaces the first painting of a real story with the fixture bunny with large captions drawn over it ([the picture](../screens/20261012-IST-picture-with-words-drill-input.png): \"HAPPY BUNNY\", \"SHARE THE\", \"CARROT!\"); everything else is the real painter, the real vision judge and the real repair. Trace `c2a67d3482bbdff5beb6df58a4daf92b` (tag `chaos`): **the vision judge marked the picture of page 3 a violation of `image_no_text`, the agent said \"picture did not pass; painting it once more\", and the second picture passed.** Pages 7 and 8 went the same way with pictures from the real painter (violation, repainted, pass), so seven paintings made three repaints; the story shipped. The `verify:image_no_text` spans are in the trace and neatlogs' detection \"Picture has words painted in\" counted the trace.\n\n## Limits, said plainly'''),\n])\nsub(\"docs/TOOLS.md\", [(\"the picture-words detection now has spans to read (its pattern matches a violation and not a pass; it has not fired because no picture had painted words).\",\n \"the picture-words detection now has spans to read and **has fired**: on a drill that paints words into a real story's picture (`scripts/drill_picture_words.py`, trace `c2a67d3482bbdff5beb6df58a4daf92b`) the vision judge flagged it, the agent repainted it, and neatlogs counted one occurrence ([HR-016](../evidence/hardening/HR-016.md)).\")])\nsub(\"docs/TOOLS.md\", [(\"the trace export endpoint answered `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`,\", \"the trace export endpoint answered `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` (the full span lists were saved through the MCP instead: `scripts/save_trace_spans.py`),\")])\nsub(\"hackathon.md\", [(\"the picture-words detection has not fired (no picture had painted words); \", \"\"),\n (\"- Tests that ran: 106 backend\", \"- Picture-words detection proven: a drill that paints words into one real picture (`scripts/drill_picture_words.py`) was flagged by the vision judge, repainted, and counted by neatlogs' detection (1 occurrence, trace `c2a67d34...`). The \\\"before\\\" trace of HR-016 was recovered through the MCP (208 spans, 2 of 4 `illustrate`, no picture checks). The two cfo.ai Version-history screenshots were filed in `evidence/cfo/`. A recorded walkthrough of the app is in `evidence/demo/`; the three dashboards are for the builder to record ([DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md](docs/DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md)).\\n- Tests that ran: 106 backend\")])\nsub(\"docs/STATUS.md\", [(\"| **cfo.ai UI steps** | The workbooks are saved (`evidence/cfo/workbook/`, five files); the Version-history screenshot is not | Screenshot Version history (change 275839) into `evidence/cfo/` |\",\n \"| **cfo.ai UI steps** | Done: the workbooks (`evidence/cfo/workbook/`) and two Version-history screenshots (12 Oct, `evidence/cfo/`) are saved | none |\")])\nPYEOF\npython \"$TEMP/hr16b.py\" && echo ok","description":"Record the detection proof and file updates in docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":308307,"output_tokens":1903,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1903,"cache_read_input_tokens":308307,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019D9V1a5z1Pn2Jcd8BGqVNa":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && cat > \"$TEMP/hr16b.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef sub(p, pairs):\n    f = Path(p); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60])\n        s = s.replace(a, b, 1)\n    f.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\")\n\nsub(\"evidence/hardening/HR-016.md\", [\n (\"the verdict spans exist; its pattern matches a violation verdict and not a pass; **no story in these runs had a picture with words, so it has not fired** |\",\n  \"**fired**: on the picture-words drill (below) neatlogs counted 1 