{"parentUuid":"126220b2-d94c-4a94-97e4-8b74516ed093","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"419f33fc-96f6-4c2c-b1fc-7ed7e9517d67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPzSnwbCoLrcfJeowEomYQ","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/WEB.md:69:pictures and voices that have not arrived show a gentle \"Pip is still painting\", and ones that never arrive (a `degraded` event, or\ndocs/DESIGN.md:9:1. **The oath comes first.** Before any story text exists, the agent writes a list of promises for this drawing and lesson. A fixed core is always present; the model may add promises, never remove or relax one. The oath is hashed and recorded before the first page.\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:125:- **Performance:** preload the next page's image and audio; WebP/AVIF; scene images ≤ ~250 KB on mobile; lazy-load the rest; the first page appears while later ones are still being generated (four pages then four, driven by the real graph).\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:167:The page images appear as soon as the agent has them; a page whose image failed shows a friendly paper-cut placeholder and the text still works (the failure is a recorded commitment, not a blank).\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:190:| Generation takes 3+ minutes | Pip: \"This one is a big story!\"; the first pages open as soon as they exist |\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:255:- **A 10-minute usability test with a real child of 4–8, with a parent present and consent** (if one is available): can they get from Welcome to the first page unaided; can they pick a choice on the first try; do they find the Grown-ups area; do they get stuck anywhere. Target: first-try tap success ≥ 90% on primary targets, zero help needed to start. Do not record the child; never put the child's drawing in a trace or a post.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f4b027ed-901c-4e24-8e52-ee88255e89e4","timestamp":"2026-10-12T09:02:29.182Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/WEB.md:69:pictures and voices that have not arrived show a gentle \"Pip is still painting\", and ones that never arrive (a `degraded` event, or\ndocs/DESIGN.md:9:1. **The oath comes first.** Before any story text exists, the agent writes a list of promises for this drawing and lesson. A fixed core is always present; the model may add promises, never remove or relax one. The oath is hashed and recorded before the first page.\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:125:- **Performance:** preload the next page's image and audio; WebP/AVIF; scene images ≤ ~250 KB on mobile; lazy-load the rest; the first page appears while later ones are still being generated (four pages then four, driven by the real graph).\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:167:The page images appear as soon as the agent has them; a page whose image failed shows a friendly paper-cut placeholder and the text still works (the failure is a recorded commitment, not a blank).\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:190:| Generation takes 3+ minutes | Pip: \"This one is a big story!\"; the first pages open as soon as they exist |\ndocs/planning/frontend.md:255:- **A 10-minute usability test with a real child of 4–8, with a parent present and consent** (if one is available): can they get from Welcome to the first page unaided; can they pick a choice on the first try; do they find the Grown-ups area; do they get stuck anywhere. Target: first-try tap success ≥ 90% on primary targets, zero help needed to start. Do not record the child; never put the child's drawing in a trace or a post.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d28af622-b8d8-49e1-a1ad-9d3537d9fa94","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/d/storybound/web","root":"/d/storybound","branch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":18,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":14},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"hatif03/storybound","visibility":"public"},"push_remote