{"parentUuid":"ead44454-70a2-4c29-89b6-65216f95006a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxA3j13nGRByMiGowcfF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JUfcnPiGwGjB4vFq8ieMmh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && printf 'evidence/demo/*.mp4\\nevidence/demo/*.webm\\n' >> .gitignore && du -sh evidence/demo/voiceover && cat > \"$TEMP/guide.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf = Path(\"docs/DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md\"); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\na = s.index(\"## 1. Our app (made for you)\")\nb = s.index(\"## 2. neatlogs dashboard\")\nnew = '''## 1. Our app (made for you, with sound and a voice-over)\nFiles in `evidence/demo/` (large video files are not committed; they stay on your disk):\n- `app-walkthrough.mp4`: the whole recording at normal speed (about 14 minutes, 1440 x 810), with every sound the app made (Pip's voice, the narration of each page, the chimes, the quiet music) and a voice-over that explains what is happening.\n- `app-walkthrough-cut.mp4`: the same with the waiting stretches (while the agent writes and checks the story, and while a page waits for its picture and voice) sped up 12 times and silent; about 9 minutes. Use this as the starting point, then cut it to about 45 seconds for the 3:00 video.\n- `app-walkthrough-cues.txt`: what happens when, in the full-length file, for cutting by hand. `voiceover/` holds each voice-over line as its own mp3 and the text of each line (`manifest.json`), so you can re-record any line in your own voice and drop it in.\n\nIt is a real story, made while the recording runs (real models, about $0.45), not a mock. Every screen is shown only when everything for it exists (words, picture, voice), so the recording holds on Pip's making screen while pages are made; the cut speeds those holds up.\n\nWhat the recording shows, in order:\n| Moment | What is on screen | What the voice-over says |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome | The home screen | What Storybound is, and that an agent checks every page against promises it wrote first |\n| Drawing | A bunny drawn with the mouse | The child draws on the screen |\n| Name, lesson | Pip picks a name; the lesson \"Sharing\"; a grown-up promise typed in | A grown-up chooses the lesson and can add a promise |\n| Making your story | Pip, the hero, and the promises filling in | The oath, writing and checking each page, rewriting a page that breaks a promise, then the wait while pictures and voices are made |\n| Reading | Page 1 with its picture and voice, a choice, a wrong answer or a right answer | A wrong answer is never a scolding |\n| Pages 2 to 8 | Each page with its picture, narration, choices | Each page was checked; nothing is shown before it is complete |\n| Quiz, order game, end | Four verified questions, the picture-order game, the talk-about card | Quiz questions that fail a check are dropped |\n| Grown-ups, receipt | The sum gate and the receipt | How many promises were checked, pages rewritten, what could not be kept |\n| Forget | The story deleted | The app forgets the story |\n\nTo make it again: start the server (`.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m uvicorn storybound.api:app --app-dir src --port 8000`), `.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe scripts\\\\make_demo_voiceover.py` (only when the words in `web/scripts/demo-voiceover.json` change), `cd web; node scripts\\\\record-demo.mjs`, then `.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe scripts\\\\compose_demo.py` (options: `--speed 12` for the cut). The browser that records has no sound card, so the script logs every sound the app plays with its exact time and the screen as timestamped frames; `compose_demo.py` puts each sound back at its time and turns the app's sounds down while the voice-over speaks. To use the app by hand: open http://127.0.0.1:8000, press \"Let's go\", draw with the mouse or a finger (a simple shape is fine), \"Done!\", pick a name, pick \"Sharing\", press \"Yes!\", wait for \"Read page 1!\", then read and answer; the grown-ups area is the small button in the corner (answer the multiplication to open it).\n\n---\n\n'''\ns = s[:a] + new + s[b:]\ns = s.replace(\"The app capture is already made by a script (below), so you only need to record the three dashboards.\", \"The app capture is already made by a script (below, with sound and a voice-over), so you only need to record the three dashboards.\")\nf.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nPYEOF\npython \"$TEMP/guide.py\" && echo ok","description":"Update the recording guide for the new app capture; ignore large videos in git"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":432967,"output_tokens":1926,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":273},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":337,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1926,"cache_read_input_tokens":432967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":337},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JUfcnPiGwGjB4vFq8ieMmh":{"command":"cd /d/storybound && printf 'evidence/demo/*.mp4\\nevidence/demo/*.webm\\n' >> .gitignore && du -sh evidence/demo/voiceover && cat > \"$TEMP/guide.py\" <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf = Path(\"docs/DEMO-RECORDING-GUIDE.md\"); s = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\na = s.index(\"## 1. Our app (made for you)\")\nb = s.index(\"## 2. neatlogs dashboard\")\nnew = '''## 1. Our app (made for you, with sound and a voice-over)\nFiles in `evidence/demo/` (large video files are not committed; they stay on your disk):\n- `app-walkthrough.mp4`: the whole recording at normal speed (about 14 minutes, 1440 x 810), with every sound the app made (Pip's voice, the narration of each page, the chimes, the quiet music) and a voice-over that explains what is happening.\n- `app-walkthrough-cut.mp4`: the same with the waiting stretches (while the agent writes and checks the story, and while a page waits for its picture and voice) sped up 12 times and silent; about 9 minutes. Use this as the starting point, then cut it to about 45 seconds for the 3:00 video.\n- `app-walkthrough-cues.txt`: what happens when, in the full-length file, for cutting by hand. `voiceover/` holds each voice-over line as its own mp3 and the text of each line (`manifest.json`), so you can re-record any line in your own voice and drop it in.\n\nIt is a real story, made while the recording runs (real models, about $0.45), not a mock. Every screen is shown only when everything for it exists (words, picture, voice), so the recording holds on Pip's making screen while pages are made; the cut speeds those holds up.\n\nWhat the recording shows, in order:\n| Moment | What is on screen | What the voice-over says |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Welcome | The home screen | What Storybound is, and that an agent checks every page against promises it wrote first |\n| Drawing | A bunny drawn with the mouse | The child draws on the screen |\n| Name, lesson | Pip picks a name; the lesson \"Sharing\"; a grown-up promise typed in | A grown-up chooses the lesson and can add a promise |\n| Making your story | Pip, the hero, and the promises filling in | The oath, writing and checking each page, rewriting a page that breaks a promise, then the wait while pictures and voices are made |\n| Reading | Page 1 with its picture and voice, a choice, a wrong answer or a right answer | A wrong answer is never a scolding |\n| Pages 2 to 8 | Each page with its picture, narration, choices | Each page was checked; nothing is shown before it is complete |\n| Quiz, order game, end | Four verified questions, the picture-order game, the talk-about card | Quiz questions that fail a check are dropped |\n| Grown-ups, receipt | The sum gate and the receipt | How many promises were checked, pages rewritten, what could not be kept |\n| Forget | The story deleted | The app forgets the story |\n\nTo make it again: start the server (`.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -m uvicorn storybound.api:app --app-dir src --port 8000`), `.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe scripts\\\\make_demo_voiceover.py` (only when the words in `web/scripts/demo-voiceover.json` change), `cd web; node scripts\\\\record-demo.mjs`, then `.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe scripts\\\\compose_demo.py` (options: `--speed 12` for the cut). The browser that records has no sound card, so the script logs every sound the app plays with its exact time and the screen as timestamped frames; `compose_demo.py` puts each sound back at its time and turns the app's sounds down while the voice-over speaks. To use the app by hand: open http://127.0.0.1:8000, press \"Let's go\", draw with the mouse or a finger (a simple shape is fine), \"Done!\", pick a name, pick \"Sharing\", press \"Yes!\", wait for \"Read page 1!\", then read and answer; the grown-ups area is the small button in the corner (answer the multiplication to open it).\n\n---\n\n'''\ns = s[:a] + new + s[b:]\ns = s.replace(\"The app capture is already made by a script (below), so you only need to record the three dashboards.\", \"The app capture is already made by a script (below, with sound and a voice-over), so you only need to record the three dashboards.\")\nf.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nPYEOF\npython \"$TEMP/guide.py\" && echo ok","description":"Update the recording guide for the new app capture; ignore large videos in git"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2fa1a3c1-b80f-4feb-abb4-3185054e7ac0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfxA3iXWxWBvdHWf55VUc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f8103c0-8