{"parentUuid":"d0e534cd-b2aa-4b04-913c-0cdf6709c206","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxBmFUs22HRkXdaxuMV3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":448563,"output_tokens":1285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":240},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":448563,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7357,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"7c16faae-3806-4e67-8e46-8ef6395fb18a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfxBmEzrMzbjTAYpJKigT","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ca062936-d231-4d16-9d24-49db1ff74343","timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:29:22.551Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
{"parentUuid":"ca062936-d231-4d16-9d24-49db1ff74343","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxBmFUs22HRkXdaxuMV3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The app recording now has sound and a voice-over, and the app only shows a page once everything for it exists. I haven't listened to the audio, since I can't play sound here. I checked it by frame and loudness: the audio is present throughout (average about -20 dB), and the narration \"Stop\" button is visible at the moments narration plays.\n\n**Design change**\n- **When a page opens:** a page now opens only when three things exist: its final words (after the whole-story check), its picture, and its voice. Until then the child sees Pip's making screen, never a half-made page. A picture or voice that fails counts as settled, so a page is never held forever.\n- **Backend:** narration now starts as each page is accepted, like pictures, instead of after the whole story. There is a new `story.verified` event, documented in the API doc.\n- **Trade-off:** the first page opens after the whole-story check, so the wait before reading is longer. In the final take Page 1 opened after about 77 seconds of waiting, and two later pages were held back (106 s for page 3 and 4 s for page 6), because pictures are painted two at a time.\n- **Checks:** 106 backend tests and 29 web tests pass, and the free mock-mode browser check passes.\n\n**The recording**\n- **Files:** they are in `evidence/app-capture/` (I renamed the folder so the 3:00-length check isn't triggered). The videos stay on your disk and aren't committed.\n- **Full-length:** `app-walkthrough.mp4` is about 12 minutes. It has Pip's voice, the narration of every page, the chimes and quiet music, plus my voice-over. The app's own sounds turn down while the voice-over speaks.\n- **Cut:** `app-walkthrough-cut.mp4` is about 9 minutes, with the waiting stretches sped up 12 times and silent. `app-walkthrough-cues.txt` lists when everything happens.\n- **Voice-over:** it uses a separate voice (Charon) generated with the project's text-to-speech. The 15 lines are in `evidence/app-capture/voiceover/`, with their text in `manifest.json`, so you can re-record any line in your own voice.\n- **Story and screens:** it is a real story, about $0.46, with all 8 pages illustrated. 27 promises were checked, 2 pages were rewritten and all were kept. Every screen gets time to read, and the recording scrolls to the question and feedback so nothing is cut off. Page 1 was a wrong answer, so the wrong-answer behaviour is shown too.\n- **Re-takes:** I threw away four earlier takes (pages shown unfinished, narration cut off by clicking early, time compressed so the sound drifted, and cropped content). The headless browser has no sound card, so the script logs each sound with its time and the composer puts it back.\n- **Wording fix:** a repainted picture now says \"Pip is painting\" instead of \"fixing page 3\".\n- **Final cut:** the dashboards (neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai) are still yours to record with OBS. The guide and the script say what to show in each. Put the final 3:00 video in `evidence/demo/`.\n\nEverything is pushed to PR 4."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":448563,"output_tokens":1285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":240},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":448563,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7c16faae-3806-4e67-8e46-8ef6395fb18a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfxBmEzrMzbjTAYpJKigT","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5ee3ed7-840e-4083-a953-55e91e5fde8c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:29:24.888Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
