{"parentUuid":"930c8ff0-7b51-40ae-aa25-257973202903","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"24653995-258f-4147-895a-48045f20a23b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Also in the design i see a listen button, no child will actually click on it every time for every screen, make it such that as sonn as someone gone on the screen, the image is already there and with some wait time the story starts playing itself, the button still be there to replay the narration after it finishes as many time as someone wants.\n\nI have gotten this message form the neatlogs team:\n\n<pasted_content id=\"f327\">\nHey everyone!\n\nWe're getting close. 👀\n\nneatHack submissions open today, October 12, from 7:00 to 11:55 PM IST.\n\nA few things to get ready before the window opens:\n\nYour team name and project description\n\nA public GitHub repo with your code\n\nA demo video showing what you've built\n\nHere's how to submit\n\n1. Quote-tweet the official @neatlogs launch post on X.\n\nWe'll share the link at 7 PM IST.\n\nYour quote-tweet must tag @neatlogs, @EntireHQ, and @arithecfo in the quote-tweet.\n\n2. Fill out the submission form.\n\nWe'll share that link too.\n\n⚠️ Important: Both steps are required. You must quote-tweet the official launch post and tag all three accounts. Our systems use these to detect your submission. If you only fill out the form, or miss the required tags, your submission won't be detected.\n\n⭐ Bonus points: Use your demo video to clearly explain the problem you're solving and how your solution works.\n\n🔥 We’ll engage with the first 50 quote-tweets, so it's worth getting everything ready ahead of time.\n\nWe'll share the links when submissions open. Keep an eye on Discord for updates and any final cutoff changes.\n\nGood luck! Can't wait to see what you've been working on.\n\n— Team neatlogs\n</pasted_content id=\"f327\">\n"}]},"uuid":"a81f2ef1-1d79-474f-9345-42176e3e8528","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:09:13.872Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":34,"turnIndex":63},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"D:\\storybound","sessionId":"531bd6f2-4e0c-4a05-a2e1-9f902bd0eeb6","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"experiments/architecture-and-chaos","slug":"glimmering-splashing-ladybug"}
